t["subzone:grand-vestibule"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,255,25.455.0,26.369.0,28.149.0,29.154.0,41.249.0,44.177.0",["h"]="e3fa08",["n"]="Gran Vestíbulo",["s"]="Gran Vestíbulo. El Gran Vestíbulo es el monumental vestíbulo de entrada del Monasterio Escarlata en Claros de Tirisfal. Bordeado de pilares carmesíes y efigies de piedra de cruzados caídos, sirve como umbral donde los aventureros se preparan para penetrar en las salas interiores del monasterio. Más allá de las pesadas puertas exteriores del Monasterio se encuentra el Gran Vestíbulo, una amplia sala de mármol dedicada al orgullo marcial de la Cruzada Escarlata. Estatuas de campeones acorazados montan guardia junto a pilares de piedra abovedados, y centinelas, discípulos y augures fanáticos patrullan las losas para abatir a cualquiera que ose entrar sin el tabardo carmesí de la orden. Para los intrusos, es la primera muestra de la implacable disciplina y el fanatismo de la Cruzada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The vestibule displays the tragic corruption of Lordaeron's former holy sanctuaries, showing how devotion to the Light curdled into blind, violent fanaticism.",["race:Undead"]="Positioned just northeast of the Undercity, this grand entryway represents the frontline of the living zealots actively threatening Forsaken sovereignty in Tirisfal."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the grand entrance chamber of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, connecting the outer courtyard to the four interior wings.",["al"]={"what is this room","grand vestibule info","monastery entrance hall"},["q"]="What is the Grand Vestibule?"},{["a"]="The chamber is defended by active Scarlet Crusade personnel, primarily Scarlet Sentries, Scarlet Disciples, and Scarlet Augurs stationed to bar intruders.",["al"]={"who patrols here","vestibule mobs","crusaders in vestibule"},["q"]="What enemies guard this area?"},{["a"]="Both factions send champions into the Monastery—the Alliance seeking to reclaim Lordaeron's holy sites or purge heretics, and the Horde acting to secure Tirisfal Glades for the Forsaken. Their paths inevitably collide in this shared entrance hall.",["al"]={"pvp in vestibule","why are players fighting here","contested vestibule"},["q"]="Why do the Alliance and Horde fight here?"},{["a"]="The statues depict honored warriors and heroes of the Scarlet Crusade, sculpted in heavy plate armor to serve as enduring symbols of their unyielding crusade against the undead.",["al"]={"who are the statues","vestibule statues","crusade monuments"},["q"]="Whom do the statues in the vestibule depict?"}},["kw"]={"entrance hall","grand vestibule","scarlet augur","scarlet disciple","scarlet monastery","scarlet sentry","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Grand Vestibule",["s"]="The Grand Vestibule is the monumental entrance hall of the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades. Lined with crimson pillars and stone effigies of fallen crusaders, it serves as the threshold where adventurers prepare to breach the monastery's inner halls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Past the heavy outer gates of the Monastery lies the Grand Vestibule, an expansive marble hall dedicated to the martial pride of the Scarlet Crusade. Statues of armored champions stand vigil beside vaulted stone pillars, and zealous sentries, disciples, and augurs patrol the flagstones to strike down anyone daring to enter without the order's crimson tabard. For trespassers, it is the first taste of the Crusade's unrelenting discipline and fanaticism.",["t"]="The Threshold of Zealotry"},{["b"]="Because the vestibule sits directly outside the secured inner wings of the monastery, it functions as a perilous gathering point. Both Alliance strike teams sent north and Horde forces pushing out from the nearby Undercity converge under these high arches, turning the ornate entry into a chaotic and bloody battleground long before anyone breaches the inner cloisters.",["t"]="A Contested Meeting Ground"}}}}}
t["subzone:great-lift"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,378,35.548.0,18.430.0,25.180.0,39.252.0,32.153.0,31.143.0",["h"]="24f2af",["n"]="El Gran Elevador",["s"]="El Gran Elevador. El Gran Elevador es un enorme sistema de elevadores de ingeniería tauren situado en el extremo sur de Los Baldíos. Es la ruta principal para transportar a viajeros y suministros en un descenso de cientos de metros hasta la cuenca del escarpado cañón de Las Mil Agujas. A pesar de su valor estratégico, los agresivos jabaespines que avanzan por los páramos del sur han hecho que acercarse al borde sea cada vez más peligroso. Cruzando el escarpado borde del acantilado entre el sur de Los Baldíos y el suelo del cañón de Las Mil Agujas, El Gran Elevador se erige como una maravilla de la práctica construcción tauren. Construido con madera maciza, cuerda trenzada y poleas con contrapesos, sus plataformas emparejadas transportan caravanas, mensajeros y guerreros de forma segura a través de un precipicio vertical que, de otro modo, destrozaría cualquier carreta. En las plataformas superior e inferior, tauren como el Valiente Lunasta y Grish Largocamino montan guardia, manteniendo a los viajeros informados sobre el camino que tienen por delante y asegurándose de que la carga pase sin problemas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The lift is a vital Horde arterial link connecting central Kalimdor to the isolated reaches of Thousand Needles and Shimmering Flats.",["race:Tauren"]="Constructed with sturdy timber and counterweights, the lift showcases your people's ingenious ability to overcome rugged landscape obstacles without scarring the earth."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Great Lift was designed and constructed by the tauren to bridge the massive vertical gap between the arid plateaus of the Barrens and the deep canyon floor of Thousand Needles.",["al"]={"who made the great lift","great lift builders","tauren elevator origin"},["q"]="Who built the Great Lift?"},{["a"]="The encroaching quilboar of the southern Barrens have aggressively expanded their territory toward the rim. Their raiding parties prowl the approaches, often harassing or outright ambushing supply caravans and couriers bound for the elevator platforms.",["al"]={"why are there quilboar here","southern barrens danger","lift road blocked"},["q"]="Why is traveling to the lift dangerous?"},{["a"]="Brave Moonhorn and Grish Longrunner are stationed at the lift to watch the routes, assist Horde travelers, and keep an eye on the surrounding wilderness.",["al"]={"who guards the lift","lift keepers","tauren at the lift"},["q"]="Who watches over the Great Lift?"},{["a"]="Riding the platforms down brings travelers onto the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, while ascending leads straight into the southern Barrens.",["al"]={"where does lift go","what is below the lift","lift destination"},["q"]="Where does the Great Lift lead?"}},["kw"]={"brave moonhorn","elevator","great lift","grish longrunner","quilboar","the barrens","thousand needles"},["n"]="Great Lift",["s"]="The Great Lift is a massive, tauren-engineered elevator system perched on the southern edge of the Barrens. It serves as the primary route lowering travelers and supplies hundreds of feet into the sheer canyon basin of Thousand Needles. Despite its strategic value, aggressive quilboar encroaching through the southern wastes have made approaching the rim increasingly perilous.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning the sheer cliff edge between the southern Barrens and the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, the Great Lift stands as a marvel of practical tauren construction. Built using heavy timber, braided rope, and counterweighted pulleys, its paired platforms carry caravans, couriers, and warriors safely across a vertical precipice that would otherwise break any wagon. At the top and bottom platforms, tauren like Brave Moonhorn and Grish Longrunner maintain watch, keeping travelers informed of the road ahead and ensuring cargo passes smoothly.",["t"]="A Gateway Carved from Wood and Rope"},{["b"]="Operating the lift has become increasingly hazardous due to the hostile territory above it. Aggressive quilboar tribes in the southern Barrens have expanded aggressively southward, choking the road toward the lift and threatening to cut off Thousand Needles from the northern trails entirely. Those who make the long journey south must constantly fend off razorfen raiders before they can ever step foot onto the wooden platforms.",["t"]="Dangers at the Rim"}}}}}
t["subzone:greenpaw-village"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,367,22.495.0,24.405.0,34.157.0,30.152.0,49.210.0,45.239.0",["h"]="ee3ad2",["n"]="Poblado Zarpaverde",["s"]="Poblado Zarpaverde. Poblado Zarpaverde es un asentamiento fúrbolg ubicado en el centro de Vallefresno, situado entre el Refugio de la Algaba y el Refugio Brisa de Plata. Sirve como hogar principal de la tribu Maderiza, liderada por el jefe Murgut y el chamán Oakpaw. Atrapado por la corrupción demoníaca y asediado por fuerzas externas, el poblado es un punto de conflicto activo tanto para los viajeros de la Alianza como de la Horda. Situado al sur del Refugio de la Algaba y al noreste del Refugio Brisa de Plata, Poblado Zarpaverde fue antaño un hogar tranquilo para los habitantes úrsidos del bosque. A raíz de la Tercera Guerra, sus fúrbolgs residentes —la tribu Maderiza— sucumbieron a la insidiosa corrupción que contaminaba el suelo y los espíritus de Vallefresno. Bajo el dominio del jefe Murgut y su guía espiritual corrupto, el chamán Oakpaw, los Maderiza se han vuelto hostiles e inestables, atacando a cualquier viajero que se adentre en su territorio forestal.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids witness the pain of the ancient bear folk firsthand at Greenpaw Village, where the balance of nature has broken down into rampant feral madness.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, seeing the Foulweald succumb to corruption so near Raynewood Retreat and their sacred moonwells is a tragic reminder of Ashenvale's lingering demonic scars."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Greenpaw Village lies in central Ashenvale, directly south of Raynewood Retreat, northeast of Silverwind Refuge, and just northwest of the southern moonwell.",["al"]={"greenpaw location","where is greenpaw village","find greenpaw"},["q"]="Where is Greenpaw Village located?"},{["a"]="The settlement is populated by the Foulweald furbolg tribe, who are governed by Chief Murgut alongside their corrupted spiritual advisor, Shaman Oakpaw.",["al"]={"who is here","greenpaw mobs","greenpaw furbolgs"},["q"]="Who lives in Greenpaw Village?"},{["a"]="Like many furbolg tribes across northern Kalimdor, the Foulweald tribe fell victim to the demonic corruption left behind after the Burning Legion invaded Ashenvale, driving their minds into maddened aggression.",["al"]={"why are furbolgs mad","are greenpaw furbolgs corrupt"},["q"]="Why are the furbolgs in Greenpaw Village hostile?"},{["a"]="Both factions view the aggressive Foulweald as a threat to their roads and settlements. The night elves seek to cleanse or contain the madness near their moonwells, while Horde forces clash with the furbolgs as they push through Ashenvale.",["al"]={"greenpaw quests","who attacks greenpaw"},["q"]="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting here?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","foulweald","furbolg","greenpaw village","murgut","oakpaw","raynewood retreat","silverwind refuge"},["n"]="Greenpaw Village",["s"]="Greenpaw Village is a furbolg settlement nestled in central Ashenvale, situated between Raynewood Retreat and Silverwind Refuge. It serves as the primary home of the Foulweald tribe, led by Chief Murgut and the shaman Oakpaw. Gripped by demonic corruption and embattled by outside forces, the village is an active conflict point for both Alliance and Horde travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated south of Raynewood Retreat and northeast of Silverwind Refuge, Greenpaw Village was once a quiet home for the forest's ursine denizens. In the wake of the Third War, its resident furbolgs—the Foulweald tribe—succumbed to the insidious corruption tainting Ashenvale's soil and spirits. Under the dominion of Chief Murgut and their corrupted spiritual guide, Shaman Oakpaw, the Foulweald have become hostile and unstable, attacking any travelers who stray into their forest territory.",["t"]="A Corrupted Settlement"},{["b"]="Because of their relentless aggression and proximity to major roadways, Greenpaw Village draws hostility from every side. Alliance sentinels and night elf druids seek to purge the mad furbolgs to protect their nearby outposts and sacred moonwells. Simultaneously, Horde forces advancing into Ashenvale have fought bloody skirmishes against the Foulweald as both factions push through the ancient woodland.",["t"]="Caught in the Crosshairs"}}}}}
t["subzone:greymane-wall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,242,23.673.0,22.617.1,35.216.0,44.176.0,53.268.0,65.257.0",["h"]="889236",["n"]="La Muralla de Cringrís",["s"]="La Muralla de Cringrís. La Muralla de Cringrís es un enorme baluarte de piedra que se extiende por la frontera sur del Bosque de Argénteos. Construida por el rey Genn Cringrís tras la Segunda Guerra, aísla al reino de Gilneas del mundo exterior tras unas puertas impenetrables y cerradas a cal y canto. Tras la Segunda Guerra, el rey Genn Cringrís comenzó a resentirse con la Alianza de Lordaeron, en particular por los impuestos necesarios para mantener los campos de internamiento de orcos y construir el Castillo de Nethergarde. Al decidir que Gilneas ya había aportado suficientes monedas y sangre por problemas ajenos, Cringrís se retiró de la Alianza y ordenó erigir una colosal barrera a lo largo de la entrada de la península. Al hacerlo, abandonó tierras pertenecientes a Lord Darius Crowley —incluidas Aldea Piroleña y Molino Ámbar—, dejándolas aisladas en el lado norte de los muros. Cuando la Tercera Guerra trajo la Plaga de la no-muerte y a innumerables refugiados desesperados a sus pies, las puertas permanecieron despiadadamente atrancadas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Greymane Wall stands as a bitter reminder of Gilnean abandonment. When Lordaeron fell to the Scourge, Greymane turned a deaf ear to his former allies, leaving them to rot outside his gates.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken who now claim Silverpine Forest, the wall forms an impassable southern border, sealing away a human kingdom whose intentions and inner strength remain entirely unknown."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Behind the wall lies the peninsula kingdom of Gilneas. Ruled by King Genn Greymane, it completely isolated itself from Lordaeron and the rest of the world before the Third War, barring all commerce and communication.",["al"]={"what is behind the wall","where does greymane wall lead","what kingdom is behind the wall"},["q"]="What lies beyond the Greymane Wall?"},{["a"]="No. The massive portcullis and iron-banded doors are firmly barred from the southern side. Gilneas has severed all contact with the outside world, and nothing enters or leaves.",["al"]={"how to get past greymane wall","can you open greymane wall","open the gate"},["q"]="Can you open the gates of the Greymane Wall?"},{["a"]="The wall utilized the surrounding mountainous terrain as a natural barrier. Building along this ridge forced the kingdom to abandon the northern holdings of Lord Darius Crowley—including Pyrewood Village and Ambermill—sowing bitter domestic dissent within Gilneas.",["al"]={"why did they build it here","why cut off pyrewood","crowley lands cut off"},["q"]="Why was the wall built here instead of farther south?"},{["a"]="When the Scourge ravaged Lordaeron, masses of fleeing human refugees gathered outside the wall begging for entry. King Greymane refused to unseal the gates to protect his kingdom, and the desperate refugees were eventually slaughtered by the undead outside.",["al"]={"scourge refugees wall","refugees outside greymane wall"},["q"]="What happened to the refugees who fled here during the Third War?"}},["kw"]={"arugal","darius crowley","genn greymane","gilneas","greymane wall","pyrewood","silverpine"},["n"]="Greymane Wall",["s"]="The Greymane Wall is a massive stone bulwark spanning the southern frontier of Silverpine Forest. Built by King Genn Greymane after the Second War, it seals the kingdom of Gilneas away from the outside world behind impenetrable, locked gates.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the Second War, King Genn Greymane grew resentful of the Alliance of Lordaeron, particularly the taxes required to maintain the orc internment camps and build Nethergarde Keep. Deciding Gilneas had given enough of its coin and blood for foreign troubles, Greymane withdrew from the Alliance and ordered a colossal barrier raised across the head of the peninsula. In doing so, he abandoned lands belonging to Lord Darius Crowley—including Pyrewood Village and Ambermill—leaving them stranded on the northern side of the stones. When the Third War brought the Plague of Undeath and countless desperate refugees to its foot, the gates remained pitilessly barred.",["t"]="A Monument to Isolation"},{["b"]="While the rampart successfully kept the armies of the Scourge from overrunning the peninsula, safety brought a dark price. Gilnean forces briefly opened the gates during the war to fight the undead, only to be overwhelmed. In desperation, King Greymane ordered Archmage Arugal to summon the feral worgen. Though the beasts drove back the Scourge, they turned on their summoners. Greymane's soldiers retreated and sealed the gates shut once more, but infected fighters carried the beastly contagion back inside. Behind the cold, silent wall, internal rebellion and a creeping curse now tear the isolated kingdom apart.",["t"]="The Price of Seclusion"}}}}}
t["subzone:grim-batol"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,331,23.518.0,26.609.0,29.218.0,42.280.0,51.264.0,34.242.0",["h"]="6b36ac",["n"]="Grim Batol",["s"]="Grim Batol. Grim Batol es una antigua fortaleza montañosa enana en ruinas que se alza sobre el extremo oriental de Los Humedales. Construida por el clan Martillo Salvaje, abandonada tras una oscura maldición durante la Guerra de los Tres Martillos y ocupada más tarde por los orcos Faucedraco como guarida de cría de dragones, sus puertas selladas siguen siendo una ominosa lacra sobre las tierras altas. Tras la antigua guerra civil de los tres clanes, el thalador Khardros Martillo Salvaje excavó Grim Batol en las escarpadas montañas al este de la ciénaga. Durante la posterior Guerra de los Tres Martillos, la hechicera Hierro Negro Modgud asedió la fortaleza. Aunque Khardros la abatió, Modgud proyectó una sombra vil sobre las piedras antes de morir. La mácula persistente volvió inhabitables las salas, lo que obligó a los enanos Martillo Salvaje supervivientes a abandonar su magnífico reino y emigrar al norte, hacia Tierras del Interior.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The mountain represents the grim heights of the Second War, where the Dragonmaw clan harnessed enslaved dragons to conquer the skies before their violent ruin.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Grim Batol stands as a bitter testament to the War of the Three Hammers—a once-proud sister city to Ironforge rendered permanently unlivable by Dark Iron sorcery."},["faq"]={{["a"]="No. The colossal stone gates at the end of the mountain road remain firmly barred and inaccessible to travelers. Only its imposing gates and exterior battlements in the eastern mountains of the Wetlands can be visited.",["al"]={"can i go inside grim batol","is grim batol open","grim batol gate"},["q"]="Can players enter Grim Batol?"},{["a"]="During the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron sorceress Modgud infused the stronghold with a vile shadow curse before she was slain. The taint left behind rendered the fortress unlivable for the Wildhammers, driving them to abandon it and build Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands.",["al"]={"why did dwarves leave grim batol","wildhammer curse","modgud curse"},["q"]="Why did the Wildhammer dwarves abandon it?"},{["a"]="When the mage Rhonin and his companions shattered the Demon Soul, the captive Dragonqueen Alexstrasza was freed from her chains. Enraged by her cruel captivity, she and her brood incinerated Nekros Skullcrusher and shattered the Dragonmaw presence in the fortress.",["al"]={"dragonmaw grim batol","what happened to the orcs here","nekros skullcrusher"},["q"]="What happened to the Dragonmaw orcs who lived here?"},{["a"]="Presently, Grim Batol is an abandoned ruin. While remnants of the Dragonmaw clan and wild beasts linger in the surrounding crags, the Red Dragonflight maintains a watchful eye over the cursed mountain to ensure its dark history never repeats.",["al"]={"who owns grim batol","who lives in grim batol now"},["q"]="Who controls Grim Batol right now?"}},["kw"]={"alexstrasza","demon soul","dragonmaw","grim batol","modgud","nekros","wetlands","wildhammer"},["n"]="Grim Batol",["s"]="Grim Batol is an ancient, ruined dwarven mountain fortress looming over the eastern edge of the Wetlands. Built by the Wildhammer clan, abandoned after a dark curse during the War of the Three Hammers, and later occupied by the Dragonmaw orcs as a dragon breeding lair, its sealed gates remain an ominous blight upon the highlands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the ancient civil war of the three clans, Thane Khardros Wildhammer carved Grim Batol out of the jagged mountains east of the marsh. During the subsequent War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron sorceress Modgud laid siege to the fortress. Although Khardros struck her down, Modgud cast a foul shadow across the stones before her death. The lingering taint rendered the halls uninhabitable, forcing the surviving Wildhammer dwarves to abandon their magnificent kingdom and migrate north into the Hinterlands.",["t"]="A Fortress Twice Cursed"},{["b"]="Centuries later during the Second War, the fortress found a darker purpose when Orgrim Doomhammer dispatched the Dragonmaw clan to claim it. Led by the warlock Nekros Skullcrusher, the orcs utilized the ancient artifact known as the Demon Soul to enslave the red Dragonqueen Alexstrasza deep within the mountain's roots. Forced to hatch broods for the Horde's war effort, Alexstrasza remained chained until a small band of heroes shattered the artifact. Once freed, the enraged Dragon Aspect incinerated the orcs within, leaving Grim Batol a smoldering, desolate ruin watched closely by surviving red dragons.",["t"]="Chains of the Dragon Queen"}}}}}
t["subzone:grizzled-den"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,183,20.488.0,16.464.0,34.113.0,40.158.0,44.225.0",["h"]="944d6b",["n"]="El Cubil Pardo",["s"]="El Cubil Pardo. El Cubil Pardo es una caverna enclavada en las colinas nevadas justo al suroeste de Kharanos. Sirve como una conocida guarida para los feroces wendigos que escupen escarcha, autóctonos de Dun Morogh. Excavado en las profundidades de los riscos al suroeste de Kharanos, El Cubil Pardo es tristemente célebre entre los montañeros locales por ser el nido de las manadas de wendigos de Dun Morogh. Estas agresivas bestias simiescas usan su aliento helado contra los intrusos y se agrupan para proteger sus madrigueras. A pesar del peligro, cazadores intrépidos desafían con frecuencia las profundidades de la caverna para recolectar las densas melenas de wendigo, que alcanzan un precio respetable entre los artesanos que buscan forrar asientos fríos y carruajes con pieles aislantes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Mining"]="The outer and inner tunnels of the den hold exposed copper deposits, making it a viable early digging spot if you can keep the wendigos off your back.",["race:Dwarf"]="Clearing the Grizzled Den is practically a rite of passage for young dwarven mountaineers training around Kharanos."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Grizzled Den is found southwest of Kharanos in Dun Morogh, tucked away into the snow-covered mountain ridges.",["al"]={"grizzled den location","where is grizzled den","how to get to grizzled den"},["q"]="Where is the Grizzled Den located?"},{["a"]="The cavern is overrun with packs of ferocious wendigos. These aggressive, white-furred beasts can exhale freezing frost and will readily swarm any interloper.",["al"]={"what is in grizzled den","grizzled den mobs","creatures inside grizzled den"},["q"]="What creatures live in the Grizzled Den?"},{["a"]="Hunters and adventurers brave the den primarily to hunt wendigos for their thick manes, which are highly prized for crafting warm seat covers. Others brave the freezing tunnels to extract raw copper ore from the cavern walls.",["al"]={"why go to grizzled den","grizzled den quests","wendigo manes"},["q"]="Why do people venture into the Grizzled Den?"}},["kw"]={"cave","dun morogh","frost","grizzled den","kharanos","wendigo"},["n"]="Grizzled Den",["s"]="The Grizzled Den is a cavern nestled in the snowy hills just southwest of Kharanos. It serves as a notorious lair for the ferocious, frost-breathing wendigos indigenous to Dun Morogh.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved deep into the crags southwest of Kharanos, the Grizzled Den is notorious among local mountaineers as the nesting ground of Dun Morogh's wendigo packs. These aggressive, ape-like beasts wield frosty breath against intruders and band together to protect their hollows. Despite the peril, daring hunters regularly brave the cavern's depths to harvest thick wendigo manes, which fetch a respectable sum among craftsmen looking to line cold chairs and carriage seats with insulated fur.",["t"]="A Frost-Chilled Lair"},{["b"]="Beyond its fearsome inhabitants, the twisting tunnels of the Grizzled Den draw opportunists searching for natural wealth. Prospectors frequently venture past the outer entrance to hammer at copper veins jutting from the frozen stone walls, while adventurous scouts often scour the darker corners for discarded footlockers. However, delve too far into the inner reaches, and you are bound to face the dens' largest and most vicious predators lurking in the shadows.",["t"]="Hidden Treasures"}}}}}
t["subzone:grizzlepaw-ridge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,205,17.468.0,34.150.0,50.184.0",["h"]="b50a4e",["n"]="Fuerte Zarpagris",["s"]="Fuerte Zarpagris. Fuerte Zarpagris es una ladera escarpada y rocosa que se alza al sur de Thelsamar, en Loch Modan. Es conocida entre los montañeros locales por su densa población de osos salvajes, liderados por la legendaria bestia Ol' Sooty. Con vistas al camino al sur de Thelsamar y lindando con Valle Rompecantos al oeste, Fuerte Zarpagris es un terreno agreste dominado por fauna depredadora. Las laderas están tomadas por osos territoriales que suponen un peligro para los viajeros que bordean las montañas. En las profundidades de la cresta habita Ol' Sooty, un oso descomunal y extraordinariamente feroz temido por los cazadores locales. Los viajeros que se desplazan entre los asentamientos enanos deben vigilar de cerca la linde del bosque y las terrazas rocosas de arriba.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The ridge provides a classic proving ground for tracking wild beasts and confronting apex predators like Ol' Sooty.",["race:Dwarf"]="Perched right beside Thelsamar, the ridge's bear population represents a constant nuisance to local mountaineers and supply routes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Grizzlepaw Ridge lies in the central hills of Loch Modan, directly south of the town of Thelsamar and east of the trogg-infested Stonesplinter Valley.",["al"]={"where is grizzlepaw ridge","grizzlepaw ridge location","how to get to grizzlepaw ridge"},["q"]="Where is Grizzlepaw Ridge located?"},{["a"]="The ridge is crawling with aggressive bears. Its most infamous resident is Ol' Sooty, an exceptionally large and ferocious beast that occasionally prowls down toward the mountain base.",["al"]={"bears at grizzlepaw ridge","who is ol sooty","ol sooty loch modan"},["q"]="What dangerous creatures live on Grizzlepaw Ridge?"}},["kw"]={"bears","grizzlepaw ridge","loch modan","ol' sooty","sooty","thelsamar"},["n"]="Grizzlepaw Ridge",["s"]="Grizzlepaw Ridge is a rugged, craggy hillside rising south of Thelsamar in Loch Modan. It is notorious among local mountaineers for its dense population of wild bears, led by the legendary beast Ol' Sooty.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking the road south of Thelsamar and bordering Stonesplinter Valley to the west, Grizzlepaw Ridge is rough country dominated by predatory wildlife. The slopes are claimed by territorial bears that pose a hazard to travelers skirting the mountains. Deep within the ridge dwells Ol' Sooty, a massive and unusually fierce bear feared by local hunters. Travelers moving between the dwarven settlements must keep a wary eye on the tree line and rocky terraces above.",["t"]="Home of the Bears"}}}}}
t["subzone:grol-dom-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,270,28.428.0,25.401.0,22.195.0,27.199.0,37.222.0,27.188.0",["h"]="da64d2",["n"]="Granja de Grol'dom",["s"]="Granja de Grol'dom. La Granja de Grol'dom es una modesta hacienda orca situada en el norte de Los Baldíos, junto al camino que une Durotar y El Cruce. Habitada por Kranal Fiss y su familia, la granja cría cerdos en las áridas llanuras a pesar del constante acoso de los agresivos jabaespines locales. Establecida tras la colonización de Durotar, la Granja de Grol'dom representa los primeros esfuerzos de la Horda por cultivar la seca extensión de Los Baldíos. Atendida por el orco Kranal Fiss y sus hijos, la pequeña hacienda cría principalmente cerdos mientras desafía a la dura fauna y a los agresivos asaltantes jabaespines Crines de Acero que rondan las crestas cercanas. Es un puesto remoto y austero que proporciona un sustento vital a la emergente nación orca.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="For initiates walking the elemental path, Grol'dom Farm is a vital milestone where Kranal Fiss guides you through the dangerous rites required to commune with the spirits of fire.",["faction:Horde"]="Homesteads like Grol'dom Farm showcase the grit required by early Horde settlers trying to carve a sustainable life out of the harsh, untamed Barrens."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Grol'dom Farm is an orcish swine farm located in the northern Barrens. Established after the founding of Orgrimmar, it serves as a remote homestead worked by the orc Kranal Fiss and his children.",["al"]={"groldom farm info","what is this place barrens","orc pig farm"},["q"]="What is Grol'dom Farm?"},{["a"]="The farm is tended by an orc named Kranal Fiss along with his children. Together they maintain the pens, herd the pigs, and defend their meager livelihood against roving beasts and quillboar raiders.",["al"]={"who is at groldom farm","who lives here","kranal fiss home"},["q"]="Who lives at Grol'dom Farm?"},{["a"]="Kranal Fiss possesses knowledge of elemental rites. Orc and tauren shaman are routinely sent to speak with him during their early training to undergo trials necessary to earn their Call of Fire and manifest the Fire Totem.",["al"]={"shaman fire quest","why come to groldom","kranal fiss shaman"},["q"]="Why do shamans come to Grol'dom Farm?"},{["a"]="The surrounding savannah is infested with the Razormane tribe of quillboars. These aggressive raiders constantly harass the farm, threatening the livestock and endangering Kranal's family.",["al"]={"why are there quillboars","who attacks groldom","farm enemies"},["q"]="What threats face the farm?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","fire totem","grol'dom farm","groldom","kranal fiss","pig farm","razormane","swine"},["n"]="Grol'dom Farm",["s"]="Grol'dom Farm is a modest orcish homestead situated in the northern Barrens along the road between Durotar and the Crossroads. Inhabited by Kranal Fiss and his family, the farm raises swine in the arid plains despite constant harassment from aggressive local quillboars.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Established following the settlement of Durotar, Grol'dom Farm represents the Horde's early efforts to farm the dry expanse of the Barrens. Tended by the orc Kranal Fiss and his children, the small homestead primarily raises pigs while braving the harsh wildlife and aggressive Razormane quillboar raiders that prowl the nearby ridges. It is a lonely, rugged outpost that supplies vital sustenance to the emerging orcish nation.",["t"]="A Swine Farm in the Savannah"},{["b"]="Beyond its mundane function as a pig farm, the homestead holds quiet importance for Horde initiates on the spiritual path. Kranal Fiss possesses deep knowledge of elemental rites and plays a key role in guiding young shaman through their trials. Seekers traveling west from Orgrimmar are regularly directed to this humble farm to learn the secrets necessary to commune with the primal spirits of fire.",["t"]="A Beacon for Young Shaman"}}}}}
t["subzone:grommash-hold"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,255,24.481.0,23.405.0,28.165.0,30.233.0,43.229.0,49.140.0",["h"]="c9f555",["n"]="Fuerte Grommash",["s"]="Fuerte Grommash. Fuerte Grommash es la sede fortificada del Jefe de Guerra Thrall, enclavada en lo alto de los riscos rojos del Valle de la Sabiduría en Orgrimmar. Nombrada en honor al sacrificio de Grommash Grito Infernal, la fortaleza sirve como Centro de Mando y corazón político de La nueva Horda. Ubicada en el apacible Valle de la Sabiduría, Fuerte Grommash sirve como corte real y santuario estratégico de la Horda. Construido en los imponentes muros del cañón, su grueso interior de piedra se mantiene notablemente sombrío y frío, una elección deliberada del Jefe de Guerra Thrall para mantener a emisarios, peticionarios y señores de la guerra alerta y serenos durante las audiencias. Aquí, Thrall delibera sobre la defensa de Kalimdor, guiado por veteranos consejeros como Eitrigg y visitado por líderes raciales como Vol'jin.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="This is the very heart of the Horde's sovereignty, where treaties are forged and campaigns against threats across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms are directed.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, the hold and Mannoroth's remains outside are the ultimate testament to their liberation from the demonic blood curse by the sacrifice of Grom Hellscream."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Warchief Thrall holds court here, alongside key Horde leaders and advisors including the orcish elder Eitrigg, the Darkspear leader Vol'jin, and the warrior Nazgrel.",["al"]={"who is in the hold","who lives in grommash hold","who rules here"},["q"]="Who is inside Grommash Hold?"},{["a"]="It is named after Grommash 'Grom' Hellscream, the legendary chieftain of the Warsong clan. Grom struck down the pit lord Mannoroth during the Third War, paying with his life to permanently free the orcish race from demonic servitude.",["al"]={"why grommash hold","who was grommash","named after who"},["q"]="Why is it named Grommash Hold?"},{["a"]="The skull and armor belong to Mannoroth, the demon lord whose blood initially enslaved the orcs on Draenor. The remains were hauled from Ashenvale and mounted on a tree trunk outside the hold as a monument to the Horde's freedom.",["al"]={"demon skull outside","mannoroth skull","bones in front"},["q"]="What are the giant bones displayed outside?"},{["a"]="Many orcish guards and older directional signs still refer to the structure as Thrall's Fortress, after the warchief who holds court inside.",["al"]={"thrall's fortress","thralls fortress","hold vs fortress"},["q"]="Why do some city signs call it Thrall's Fortress?"}},["kw"]={"eitrigg","grommash hold","mannoroth","orgrimmar","thrall","thrall's fortress","valley of wisdom"},["n"]="Grommash Hold",["s"]="Grommash Hold is the fortified seat of Warchief Thrall, nestled high in the red cliffs of the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar. Named in honor of Grommash Hellscream's sacrifice, the fortress serves as the command center and political heart of the new Horde.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched within the tranquil Valley of Wisdom, Grommash Hold serves as the royal court and strategic sanctum of the Horde. Built into the towering canyon walls, its thick stone interior remains notably dim and chilly—a deliberate choice by Warchief Thrall to keep emissaries, petitioners, and warlords sharp and sober during audiences. Here, Thrall deliberates on the defense of Kalimdor, guided by veteran counselors like Eitrigg and visited by racial chieftains such as Vol'jin.",["t"]="The Seat of the Warchief"},{["b"]="Just outside the stronghold rests the shattered armor and horned skull of the pit lord Mannoroth, mounted upon the trunk of an ancient tree. Placed there to honor Grom Hellscream, who traded his life to slay the demon in Ashenvale, the memorial stands as both a proud symbol of the orcs' liberation from the demonic blood curse and a permanent, solemn warning against falling into reckless savagery again.",["t"]="The Monument to Freedom"}}}}}
t["subzone:grove-of-the-ancients"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,274,25.440.0,20.434.0,35.138.0,11.195.0,31.177.0,33.182.0",["h"]="f2ccd7",["n"]="Páramo de los Ancestros",["s"]="Páramo de los Ancestros. El Páramo de los Ancestros es un santuario sagrado de los elfos de la noche situado entre las ruinas de un antiguo templo en el sureste de Costa Oscura. Enclavado junto al Río Culebra, este sereno refugio sirve como punto de encuentro para espíritus de la naturaleza y está custodiado por el venerable ancestro del conocimiento, Onus. Escondido cerca de las montañas del sureste de Costa Oscura, el Páramo de los Ancestros se erige como un remanso de paz rodeado por las antiguas piedras de un templo. A través de su corazón fluyen las agitadas aguas del Río Culebra, proporcionando un tranquilo refugio en medio de una costa cada vez más asolada por la corrupción y una fauna inquieta. La arboleda sirve como lugar de reunión para el Círculo de los Ancestros, donde los espíritus de la naturaleza y los kaldorei velan por el delicado equilibrio del bosque.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The grove is a revered natural sanctuary, offering druids a direct connection to the wisdom of the Ancient of Lore Onu and the spirits of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="Surrounded by ancient temple ruins and tended by nature spirits, the grove serves as a solemn reminder of long-standing kaldorei harmony with the land."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The grove is located in the southeastern region of Darkshore, nestled against the mountain foothills near the banks of the Wildbend River.",["al"]={"grove of ancients location","where is grove of the ancients","onu location"},["q"]="Where is the Grove of the Ancients?"},{["a"]="Onu is a wise Ancient of Lore residing in the grove. He acts as an elder guide, watching over the southeastern woods and advising druids and travelers attempting to mend the balance of Darkshore.",["al"]={"who is onu","ancient in grove of ancients","tree guy darkshore"},["q"]="Who is Onu?"},{["a"]="The Circle of Ancients is an assembly of great nature spirits and ancient treants who gather at the grove to commune, share knowledge, and discuss the welfare of the wild lands.",["al"]={"circle of ancients","ancients meeting darkshore"},["q"]="What is the Circle of Ancients?"},{["a"]="While the grove itself is a safe sanctuary with friendly guardians and merchants, hostile wildlife and territorial furbolg encampments lie just across the river and to the southeast.",["al"]={"grove threats","is grove safe","monsters near grove"},["q"]="Are there dangers near the grove?"}},["kw"]={"ancient of lore","circle of ancients","darkshore","grove of the ancients","onu","wildbend river"},["n"]="Grove of the Ancients",["s"]="The Grove of the Ancients is a sacred night elven sanctuary set amidst old temple ruins in southeastern Darkshore. Nestled beside the Wildbend River, this serene haven serves as a gathering ground for nature spirits and is watched over by the venerable Ancient of Lore, Onu.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away near the southeastern mountains of Darkshore, the Grove of the Ancients stands as a peaceful haven surrounded by aged temple stones. Through its heart flows the surging Wildbend River, providing a quiet refuge amidst a coastline increasingly plagued by corruption and restless wildlife. The grove serves as a meeting place for the Circle of Ancients, where nature spirits and kaldorei tend to the delicate balance of the forest.",["t"]="Sanctuary of the Wildbend"},{["b"]="The focal presence within the grove is Onu, a towering Ancient of Lore who observes the land's shifting fortunes and offers ancient wisdom to passing travelers. Alongside Onu, wandering merchants and slumbering druids find rest beneath the boughs. Though quiet, the grove lies close to territorial furbolg camps to the southeast, making it an essential frontier outpost for Alliance sentinels and druids monitoring southern Darkshore.",["t"]="Keepers and Watchers"}}}}}
t["subzone:gunther-s-retreat"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,338,29.608.0,31.204.0,41.230.0,37.249.0,49.191.0",["h"]="35c5b4",["n"]="Refugio de Gunther",["s"]="Refugio de Gunther. El Refugio de Gunther es un santuario insular aislado situado en el Lago Aguasclaras, en el centro de los Claros de Tirisfal. Sirve de refugio a Gunther Arcanos, un nigromante renegado que se liberó de la Plaga mediante pura fuerza de voluntad. Desconfiado de todos los forasteros, el eremita rodea su campamento con leales esbirros no-muertos para mantener alejados a los intrusos. Situado entre las brumosas aguas del Lago Aguasclaras, el Refugio de Gunther es un modesto campamento insular que se confunde fácilmente con otro reducto de la Plaga. Su amo, Gunther Arcanos, logró lo que pocos hechiceros mortales pudieron: al ser alzado en la no-muerte, su maestría arcana le permitió arrancar su alma del férreo control del Rey Exánime sin ninguna ayuda externa. Desconfiando de todo el mundo, Gunther asumió que el resto de los no-muertos que vagaban por Lordaeron seguían siendo marionetas de la Plaga. Se retiró a esta solitaria isla para practicar su arte en paz, apostando centinelas zombi para despedazar a cualquiera que cruce las aguas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Arcanists will appreciate Gunther's rare feat; his magical will was formidable enough to sever the Lich King's mental grip entirely unassisted.",["race:Undead"]="Gunther Arcanus mirrors the Forsaken's own tragedy: free from the Lich King, yet suspicious and guarded against a world he assumes remains in thrall to the Scourge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The island is inhabited by Gunther Arcanus, a powerful necromancer who broke free of the Lich King's control under his own power. He resides there alongside a retinue of undead thralls who guard his camp.",["al"]={"gunther island","who is on the island","gunther's retreat master"},["q"]="Who lives at Gunther's Retreat?"},{["a"]="Gunther Arcanus believes that every other undead being in Tirisfal is still enslaved by the Scourge. Because he values his independence above all else, his minions are commanded to attack anyone who approaches the island on sight.",["al"]={"why does gunther attack","why hostile","is gunther scourge"},["q"]="Why are the undead on the island hostile?"},{["a"]="Initially, no. While technically a free-willed undead like the Forsaken, Gunther isolates himself entirely. The authorities in the Undercity seek to prove to him that they too are free of the Lich King's grasp and recruit his talents to their cause.",["al"]={"is gunther in the horde","gunther forsaken","gunther undercity"},["q"]="Is Gunther aligned with the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="Just off the southwestern edge of Gunther's Retreat lies a tiny, unnamed islet known as Lillith's Dinner Table, a curious and eerie landmark resting quietly in the waters of Brightwater Lake.",["al"]={"lillith dinner table","small island near gunther","table island"},["q"]="What is the small islet southwest of the retreat?"}},["kw"]={"brightwater lake","gunther arcanus","gunther's retreat","lich","lillith's dinner table","tirisfal glades","undead"},["n"]="Gunther's Retreat",["s"]="Gunther's Retreat is an isolated island sanctuary set in Brightwater Lake in central Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the refuge of Gunther Arcanus, a renegade necromancer who broke free from the Scourge through raw willpower. Distrustful of all outsiders, the recluse surrounds his campsite with loyal undead minions to keep intruders away.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated amid the misty waters of Brightwater Lake, Gunther's Retreat is an unassuming island encampment easily mistaken for another pocket of the Scourge. Its master, Gunther Arcanus, achieved what few mortal sorcerers could: when raised in undeath, his arcane mastery allowed him to tear away his soul from the Lich King's iron grip without any outside help. Mistrusting everyone, Gunther assumed the rest of the undead wandering Lordaeron were still puppets of the Scourge. He retired to this lonely isle to practice his craft in peace, posting zombie sentinels to tear apart anyone who crosses the water.",["t"]="A Recluse in Brightwater Lake"}}}}}
t["subzone:hall-of-arms"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,275,31.579.0,40.244.0,58.272.0,40.179.0,34.97.0",["h"]="5904c6",["n"]="Sala de Armas",["s"]="Sala de Armas. La Sala de Armas sirve como cuartel general del poder militar de Forjaz y como el principal arsenal del reino enano. Situado dentro de la Sala Militar, este recinto fortificado adiestra a combatientes enanos y orquesta el despliegue de blindados pesados y máquinas de guerra aéreas. Ubicada en la esquina suroriental de la Sala Militar, la Sala de Armas es el centro de mando de las fuerzas armadas de Forjaz. Además de albergar a veteranos instructores de guerreros y cazadores, esta amplia instalación sirve como un enorme depósito y base de operaciones para la guerra mecanizada. Los pesados tanques de vapor se ensamblan y mantienen in situ para reforzar los campos de batalla de la Alianza, mientras que los girocópteros y las máquinas voladoras se elevan mediante cintas transportadoras industriales y se lanzan directamente a través de pozos de acceso verticales en el techo de la caverna hacia el Aeródromo de Forjaz situado arriba.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="The facility functions as the premier gathering ground for dwarven armsmen and veterans in the capital, offering instruction and battlemaster leadership.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the Hall of Arms exemplifies Khaz Modan's union of martial discipline and mechanical ingenuity, housing the tanks and aerial squadrons that protect the mountain kingdom."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It serves as the headquarters and command center for Ironforge's military forces. It functions as both a training ground for warriors and hunters and a vital depot where war machines like steam tanks and gyrocopters are maintained and deployed.",["al"]={"what is hall of arms","hall of arms role","why hall of arms exists"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Hall of Arms?"},{["a"]="Dwarven flying machines are raised by conveyor systems and launched through vertical shafts in the ceiling directly out to the Ironforge Airfield on the mountain slopes above. This chimney is one of the only direct surface exits out of the mountain besides the main gates.",["al"]={"ceiling shaft ironforge","flying machine tunnel","where do copters go"},["q"]="Where do the flying machines launched from the ceiling go?"},{["a"]="The facility houses instructors for warriors and hunters, as well as Alliance battlemasters organizing troop movements and enlistments for wider battlefronts across the continent.",["al"]={"trainers in hall of arms","who teaches here"},["q"]="Who can I find training inside the Hall?"},{["a"]="It is located in the southeastern quadrant of Ironforge, anchoring the back of the Military Ward.",["al"]={"hall of arms location","how to get to hall of arms"},["q"]="Where is the Hall of Arms located?"}},["kw"]={"battlemasters","dwarven army","flying machines","hall of arms","ironforge","military ward","steam tanks"},["n"]="Hall of Arms",["s"]="The Hall of Arms serves as the headquarters of Ironforge's military might and the chief arsenal of the dwarven kingdom. Located within the Military Ward, this fortified compound trains dwarven combatants and orchestrates the deployment of heavy armor and aerial war machines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated in the southeastern corner of the Military Ward, the Hall of Arms is the operational command center for the armed forces of Ironforge. Beyond housing veteran trainers for warriors and hunters, the expansive facility serves as a massive depot and staging ground for mechanized warfare. Heavy steam tanks are assembled and maintained on-site to reinforce Alliance battlefields, while gyrocopters and flying machines are brought up via industrial conveyor belts and launched directly through vertical access shafts in the cavern ceiling toward the Ironforge Airfield above.",["t"]="Heart of the Mountain's Arsenal"}}}}}
t["subzone:hall-of-gears"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,267,19.407.0,26.478.0,35.184.0,50.240.0,36.227.0,34.242.0",["h"]="945792",["n"]="Sala de los Engranajes",["s"]="Sala de los Engranajes. La Sala de los Engranajes es una cámara industrial de varios niveles situada en el interior de la caída ciudad de Gnomeregan, justo después de Corredor Mecánico. En su momento un bullicioso centro de movimiento mecánico, ha caído en la ruina, inundada de lodo tóxico, mocos errantes y troggs irradiados. Ubicada justo más allá de Corredor Mecánico, la Sala de los Engranajes ilustra el catastrófico colapso de la capital de los gnomos. Dividida en dos niveles principales, las pasarelas superiores de la cámara están ocupadas por agresivos troggs irradiados que se abren paso a través de conductos de acceso derrumbados. Abajo, el suelo yace anegado en charcos de lluvia radiactiva, donde cienos corrosivos y elementales de veneno vivos proliferan en los vertidos tóxicos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="The sheer scale of the automated gearing and elevated platforms displays the pinnacle of pre-fall gnomish engineering, though now heavily corroded by radioactive fallout.",["race:Gnome"]="Seeing the massive cogs and catwalks submerged in irradiated sludge is a painful reminder of the desperate decision that poisoned the city and drove the gnome race into exile."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Hall of Gears lies deep inside the dungeon of Gnomeregan, directly following the Clockwerk Run. It connects further inward toward the Clean Zone, the Dormitory, and the Launch Bay.",["al"]={"hall of gears location","where is hall of gears","how to get to hall of gears"},["q"]="Where is the Hall of Gears located?"},{["a"]="When High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the venting of radioactive gas to repel the trogg invasion, the contaminated runoff collected in the city's low-lying machinery halls, turning the lower floor of the Hall of Gears into a toxic wasteland.",["al"]={"why is it green","radioactive waste hall of gears","what is the sludge"},["q"]="Why is the lower level full of radioactive sludge?"},{["a"]="The upper level is infested with mutated, irradiated troggs pouring through breach tunnels. The lower tier is filled with radioactive fallout slimes, oozes, and volatile poison elementals that formed from the industrial runoff.",["al"]={"hall of gears enemies","what lives in hall of gears","hall of gears mobs"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit this chamber?"},{["a"]="The upper walkways lead southwest toward the Clean Zone and the Dormitory, as well as a dead-end maintenance corridor to the southeast. The lower irradiated floor features a winding passage to the west that leads directly into the Launch Bay.",["al"]={"hall of gears exits","where to go from hall of gears"},["q"]="Where do the exits lead from here?"}},["kw"]={"clean zone","clockwerk run","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","launch bay","radioactive","troggs"},["n"]="Hall of Gears",["s"]="The Hall of Gears is a multi-tiered industrial chamber situated inside the fallen city of Gnomeregan, just past the Clockwerk Run. Once a bustling center of mechanical movement, it has fallen into ruin, flooded with toxic sludge, roaming oozes, and irradiated troggs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned just beyond the Clockwerk Run, the Hall of Gears illustrates the catastrophic collapse of the gnome capital. Divided into two main levels, the chamber's upper catwalks are held by aggressive, irradiated troggs that claw through collapsed access shafts. Below, the floor sits drenched in pools of radioactive fallout, where corrosive slimes and living poison elementals thrive in the toxic runoff.",["t"]="A Fractured Machine"},{["b"]="The chamber serves as a critical junction deep within Gnomeregan's operational quarters. From its upper walkways, paths branch toward contaminated dead ends and the relative safety of the Clean Zone and the Dormitory. Descending into the radioactive depths below eventually leads travelers through winding maintenance passages toward the Launch Bay, though navigating either floor requires cutting through the lingering horrors of Sicco Thermaplugg's devastating venting scheme.",["t"]="Pathways through the Waste"}}}}}
t["subzone:hall-of-legends"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,300,28.609.0,17.405.0,42.231.0,37.129.0,35.273.0,46.196.0",["h"]="674584",["n"]="Sala de las Leyendas",["s"]="Sala de las Leyendas. La Sala de las Leyendas es el santuario militar de élite y el cuartel de oficiales de la Horda, ubicado dentro del Valle de la Fuerza en Orgrimmar. Tras su umbral protegido, los campeones de la Horda se reúnen en torno a planes de batalla y se pertrechan con armas de primer nivel obtenidas en conflictos a lo largo de Azeroth y más allá. Situada junto a las concurridas avenidas del Valle de la Fuerza, la Sala de las Leyendas sirve como reducto privado para los oficiales veteranos de la Horda. Más allá de su entrada custodiada, estrategas y delegados de todas las facciones —como jefe Earthbind de Cima del Trueno, guardia de sangre Hini'wana de los Lanza Negra y consejero Willington de Entrañas— debaten sobre mapas de tierras en disputa y el estado militar de ambas facciones. Aquí, solo a los guerreros que han puesto a prueba su temple y alcanzado el rango de Guardia de piedra o superior se les permite el paso para reclamar el botín y el armamento dignos de su estatus.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="For front-line fighters, gaining entry to the Hall of Legends represents the pinnacle of martial respect, granting access to weapons forged in conflicts across multiple worlds.",["faction:Horde"]="The Hall of Legends is the ultimate testament to Horde military achievement, offering recognition, strategic council, and prized wargear to those who shed blood for the Warchief."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Only Horde champions who have achieved the rank of Stone Guard (Rank 6) or higher in the military honor system are granted passage through its threshold. Lower-ranking soldiers and ordinary citizens are turned away at the entrance.",["al"]={"can i enter hall of legends","hall of legends requirement","rank required for hall of legends"},["q"]="Who is allowed inside the Hall of Legends?"},{["a"]="The Hall of Legends is situated in the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar, near the city's primary barracks and administrative seat.",["al"]={"where is hall of legends","hall of legends location","how to get to hall of legends"},["q"]="Where is the Hall of Legends located?"},{["a"]="Inside lies a central strategy table flanked by military representatives of the Horde's various races, surrounded by maps of Azeroth and military records. Quartermasters also maintain armories here, distributing prestigious arms, armor, and mounts to accomplished officers.",["al"]={"what is in hall of legends","hall of legends interior"},["q"]="What is inside the Hall of Legends?"},{["a"]="Yes. The Alliance counterpart is the Champions' Hall, situated in the Old Town district of Stormwind City, which similarly serves as an officer barracks and armory for honored Alliance combatants.",["al"]={"alliance hall of legends","alliance counterpart"},["q"]="Does the Alliance have an equivalent location?"}},["kw"]={"hall of legends","officer barracks","orgrimmar","pvp","spoils of war","stone guard","valley of strength"},["n"]="Hall of Legends",["s"]="The Hall of Legends is the elite military sanctuary and officer barracks of the Horde, nestled within Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. Behind its warded threshold, champions of the Horde gather around battle plans and arm themselves with premier weapons taken from conflicts across Azeroth and beyond.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located off the bustling avenues of the Valley of Strength, the Hall of Legends serves as the private redoubt for proven officers of the Horde. Beyond its guarded entrance, strategists and delegates from across the factions—including Chieftain Earthbind of Thunder Bluff, Blood Guard Hini'wana of the Darkspear, and Advisor Willington of the Undercity—confer over maps of contested lands and the military standing of both factions. Here, only warriors who have tested their mettle and achieved the rank of Stone Guard or higher are permitted entry to claim the spoils and armaments befitting their status.",["t"]="Sanctuary of Horde Champions"},{["b"]="More than just an officer lounge, the hall houses armories containing battle-tested wargear from across Azeroth and the orcs' shattered homeworld of Draenor. Many of these weapons were claimed as spoils from the ongoing clashes against the Alliance and other adversaries. For those climbing the martial ranks, it represents the physical manifestation of Horde honor, martial prowess, and hard-won victory.",["t"]="The Spoils of War"}}}}}
t["subzone:hall-of-mysteries"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,341,27.605.0,45.289.0,26.230.0,59.266.0,49.211.0",["h"]="a113cf",["n"]="Sala de los Misterios",["s"]="Sala de los Misterios. Enclavado en la Sala Mística de Forjaz, la Sala de los Misterios sirve como el corazón espiritual y erudito de la ciudad para lo arcano y lo divino. En su interior iluminado con tonos azules, practicantes enanos y gnomos estudian textos antiguos, se instruyen en los misterios de la Luz Sagrada y tejen encantamientos arcanos lejos del estruendo de la Gran Fundición. Iluminado por una característica luminiscencia azul y púrpura, la Sala de los Misterios destaca enormemente frente al resto de Forjaz. Mientras que la ciudad que lo rodea prospera sobre la piedra, el hierro y las armaduras pesadas, los cinco imponentes pilares del recinto cobijan a eruditos ataviados con suaves y vaporosas togas. Une tanto la hechicería arcana como la devoción sagrada, sirviendo de cuartel general para el sacerdocio enano y la Orden de la Mano de Plata en Khaz Modan. Aquí, jóvenes clérigos y caballeros estudian textos sagrados como el Libro de la Divinidad y reciben orientación antes de que sus viajes los lleven hacia la Catedral de la Luz de Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="For dwarven champions of the Silver Hand, the hall is a foundation of their calling, where masters assign trials of virtue and grant access to the sacred Tome of Divinity.",["class:Priest"]="High Priest Rohan guides acolytes of the Light through spiritual lessons here before sending promising priests south to confer with the leadership in Stormwind."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Hall of Mysteries is Ironforge's foremost center for both divine devotion and arcane learning. It serves as a temple for the Holy Light and a study hall where dwarven and gnomish priests, paladins, and mages gather to practice their crafts, research old scripture, and train newcomers.",["al"]={"what is this place","hall of mysteries purpose","why visit hall of mysteries"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Hall of Mysteries?"},{["a"]="High Priest Rohan oversees the priesthood within the hall, serving as the spiritual guide for dwarven practitioners of the Light, alongside paladin mentors such as Valgar Highforge who direct the city's knights of the Silver Hand.",["al"]={"who runs hall of mysteries","priest leader ironforge","who is high priest rohan"},["q"]="Who leads the clergy here?"},{["a"]="While Stormwind's Cathedral of Light is dedicated purely to the holy faith and grand ceremonial worship, the Hall of Mysteries seamlessly blends holy study with arcane scholarship under one roof. Its atmosphere is scholarly and quiet rather than strictly liturgical.",["al"]={"cathedral of light vs hall of mysteries","is it like stormwind cathedral"},["q"]="How does it compare to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="Yes. Dwarven paladins are sent to the hall to study the Tome of Divinity under the mentorship of the Silver Hand, receiving instruction and sacred trials designed to test their compassion, devotion, and courage.",["al"]={"paladin quests ironforge","tome of divinity ironforge","dwarf paladin quests"},["q"]="Can paladins complete their training trials here?"}},["kw"]={"hall of mysteries","ironforge","mage","mystic ward","paladin","priest","rohan","silver hand","tome of divinity"},["n"]="Hall of Mysteries",["s"]="Tucked into the Mystic Ward of Ironforge, the Hall of Mysteries serves as the city's spiritual and scholarly heart for the arcane and the divine. Within its blue-lit interior, dwarven and gnomish practitioners study ancient texts, train in the mysteries of the Holy Light, and weave arcane enchantments far from the clang of the Great Forge.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Illuminated by a distinctive blue and purple luminescence, the Hall of Mysteries stands out starkly against the rest of Ironforge. While the city around it thrives on stone, iron, and heavy plate, the hall's five soaring pillars shelter scholars draped in soft, flowing robes. It bridges both arcane wizardry and holy devotion, serving as the headquarters for the dwarven priesthood and the Order of the Silver Hand within Khaz Modan. Here, young clerics and knights study holy texts like the Tome of Divinity and receive guidance before their journeys carry them onward to Stormwind's Cathedral of Light.",["t"]="A Temple of Magic and Faith"}}}}}
t["subzone:hall-of-the-brave"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,246,21.443.0,45.254.0,39.151.0,33.146.0",["h"]="ba6a43",["n"]="Sala de los Valientes",["s"]="Sala de los Valientes. La Sala de los Valientes es el gran cuartel de guerreros situado en los altos orientales del Valle del Honor de Orgrimmar. Sirve como el principal complejo de entrenamiento y sede para los combatientes de primera línea, instructores y maestros de batalla de la Horda. Con vistas a las tranquilas aguas y los círculos de entrenamiento del Valle del Honor, la Sala de los Valientes sirve como un centro militar vital para la creciente Horda. En su interior, oficiales veteranos y curtidos guerreros instruyen a los iniciados en los brutales fundamentos del combate cuerpo a cuerpo, el dominio de las actitudes y la disciplina. El salón está repleto de muñecos de entrenamiento y armamento, y alberga a maestros de batalla que organizan a los combatientes para grandes enfrentamientos militares por todo Azeroth.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="The Hall of the Brave is your martial home in the capital, housing trainers who unlock advanced stances and battle maneuvers as your prowess grows.",["faction:Horde"]="This barracks stands as a living demonstration of the Horde's frontline discipline, housing battlemasters who muster troops to fight across the continent."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It serves as the main barracks and guild hall for warriors in Orgrimmar. Here, warriors learn their techniques from veteran trainers, hone their strikes on practice dummies, and consult battlemasters regarding military deployments across contested lands.",["al"]={"what is hall of the brave","what is this building","hall of the brave purpose"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Hall of the Brave?"},{["a"]="The Hall of the Brave is situated on the eastern side of the Valley of Honor, nestled along the red canyon walls overlooking the valley's central pond.",["al"]={"where is hall of the brave","hall of the brave location","find warrior trainer orgrimmar"},["q"]="Where in Orgrimmar is the hall located?"},{["a"]="The hall houses various warrior class trainers, battlemasters coordinating large-scale conflicts, and Horde grunts resting between active patrols.",["al"]={"who is in hall of the brave","hall of the brave npcs"},["q"]="Who can be found inside the hall?"}},["kw"]={"barracks","battlemaster","hall of the brave","orgrimmar","valley of honor","warrior trainer","warriors guild"},["n"]="Hall of the Brave",["s"]="The Hall of the Brave is the grand warrior barracks situated in the eastern heights of Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. It serves as the primary training compound and guild house for the Horde's front-line combatants, drillmasters, and battlemasters.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking the tranquil waters and training rings of the Valley of Honor, the Hall of the Brave serves as a vital military hub for the burgeoning Horde. Inside, veteran officers and seasoned warriors instruct initiates in the brutal fundamentals of melee combat, stance mastery, and discipline. The hall is lined with training dummies and armaments, housing battlemasters who organize combatants for major military engagements across Azeroth.",["t"]="The Warriors' Bastion"}}}}}
t["subzone:helm-s-bed-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,328,23.514.0,59.157.0,41.227.0,18.193.0,56.188.0",["h"]="7a8736",["n"]="Lago de Helm",["s"]="Lago de Helm. El Lago de Helm es una masa de agua congelada ubicada en las colinas del sureste de Dun Morogh. Un agujero abierto en el grueso hielo proporciona agua dulce vital a los montañeros y viajeros de la zona. Sin embargo, la orilla circundante se ha vuelto peligrosa debido a las bestias salvajes al acecho, el avance de los troggs y los hostiles infiltrados Hierro Negro. El Lago de Helm yace en calma bajo una gruesa capa de hielo invernal en el sureste de Dun Morogh. Los enanos de la zona mantienen un agujero excavado en la escarcha para extraer agua limpia y fresca. Aunque cruzar la extensión helada es bastante seguro, merodear cerca de las orillas se ha vuelto cada vez más arriesgado. Bestias salvajes deambulan por los límites, troggs desplazados hurgan por las crestas y una célula de enanos Hierro Negro hostiles se ha adueñado de un refugio abandonado justo al sur del agua, emboscando violentamente a cualquier viajero que pase por allí.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts traveling east toward Loch Modan must stay alert here, as the southward trail skirts uncomfortably close to aggressive Dark Iron ambushes.",["race:Dwarf"]="For the Ironforge dwarves, Helm's Bed Lake represents both a vital freshwater spot and an irritating security failure, as Dark Iron saboteurs and troggs push deeper into Dun Morogh's heartland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The hole in the thick ice is deliberately maintained by local dwarves to allow consistent access to fresh, unfrozen water amid Dun Morogh's sub-zero climate.",["al"]={"ice hole","water access","why is the ice broken"},["q"]="Why is there an open hole in the middle of the frozen lake?"},{["a"]="While the lake surface itself is solid, the perimeter is hunted by predatory beasts and stray troggs. To the south, an encampment of hostile Dark Iron dwarves occupies an old building and violently repels anyone who draws near.",["al"]={"threats at helms bed lake","who is attacking here","enemies nearby"},["q"]="What dangers lurk around Helm's Bed Lake?"},{["a"]="Narm Faulk is an unfortunate dwarf whose body can be found along the shoreline of Helm's Bed Lake, a grim casualty of the sudden surge of hostile threats and Dark Iron infiltrators in the area.",["al"]={"narm faulk corpse","dead dwarf near lake","dead body at helms bed lake"},["q"]="Who is Narm Faulk?"},{["a"]="They have not seized the lake outright, but an armed squad has claimed an abandoned structure just to the south, using it as a forward position to stage skirmishes into central Dun Morogh.",["al"]={"dark irons at the lake","dark iron dwarf lodge"},["q"]="Are the Dark Iron dwarves officially occupying the lake?"}},["kw"]={"dark iron","dun morogh","helm's bed lake","ice hole","narm faulk","trogg"},["n"]="Helm's Bed Lake",["s"]="Helm's Bed Lake is a frozen body of water nestled in the southeastern hills of Dun Morogh. A maintained hole in the thick ice provides crucial fresh water to local mountaineers and travelers. However, the surrounding shoreline has become perilous due to prowling wildlife, encroaching troggs, and hostile Dark Iron infiltrators.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Helm's Bed Lake sits quietly beneath a thick sheet of winter ice in southeastern Dun Morogh. Local dwarves keep an opening chopped through the frost to draw clean, fresh water. While crossing the frozen expanse is stable enough, lingering near the banks has become increasingly risky. Wild beasts wander the edges, displaced troggs scavenge along the ridges, and a cell of hostile Dark Iron dwarves has commandeered an abandoned lodge just south of the water, aggressively ambushing any travelers who pass through.",["t"]="A Treacherous Shoreline"}}}}}
t["subzone:heroes-vigil"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,356,20.458.0,20.488.0,22.195.0,47.190.0,33.201.0,38.225.0,19.180.0",["h"]="ece44a",["n"]="Vigilia de los Héroes",["s"]="Vigilia de los Héroes. La Vigilia de los Héroes es un claro tranquilo y sagrado situado en la isla central del Lago del Hito, en el este del Bosque de Elwynn. Centrado en torno a un monumento conocido como la Piedra del Recuerdo, fue dedicado a honrar a aquellos que cayeron durante la Primera Guerra. Hoy en día, sin embargo, el santuario se encuentra en gran parte desatendido por Ventormenta y está infestado de peligrosos magos renegados. Erigida tras la Primera Guerra, la Vigilia de los Héroes gira en torno a la Piedra del Recuerdo, un círculo de piedra grabado destinado a honrar a los soldados y ciudadanos masacrados durante el saqueo de Villadorada y los valles circundantes a manos de la Antigua Horda. Aunque en el pasado fue venerada como un bastión sagrado de fe y sacrificio, la vigilia ha ido escapando de la atención de los actuales gobernantes de Ventormenta, dejando sus tierras sagradas cubiertas de maleza y sin la vigilancia de los soldados del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The renegade wizards encamping on these sacred grounds practice dangerous, unregulated arts without the discipline or sanction of the Academy of Arcane Sciences.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, this sacred stone ring is a bitter reminder of the First War's blood price and the kingdom's modern failure to protect its own heritage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Heroes' Vigil is a monument located on the island in Stone Cairn Lake in eastern Elwynn Forest. It consists of a stone ring and memorial dedicated to honoring the fallen victims of the First War.",["al"]={"heroes vigil","what is heroes vigil","island shrine elwynn"},["q"]="What is Heroes' Vigil?"},{["a"]="The Stone of Remembrance was placed in memory of the fallen citizens and defenders who perished when the orcish Horde sacked Goldshire and ravaged eastern Elwynn Forest during the First War.",["al"]={"stone of remembrance","monument meaning","what is the stone of remembrance"},["q"]="What does the Stone of Remembrance commemorate?"},{["a"]="The island and the vigil have been occupied by hostile rogue wizards. These rogue spellcasters operate outside the law of the Kingdom of Stormwind and the oversight of established magical institutions.",["al"]={"who is at heroes vigil","heroes vigil enemies","wizards on lake"},["q"]="Who controls Heroes' Vigil today?"},{["a"]="With King Varian Wrynn missing and the realm stretched thin handling internal dissent, brigands, and monster incursions, remote shrines like Heroes' Vigil have been left undefended and largely forgotten by the ruling regency.",["al"]={"why is it abandoned","why did stormwind forget it","forgotten shrine"},["q"]="Why has Stormwind neglected the vigil?"},{["a"]="Henze Faulk is a fallen traveler whose lifeless body lies abandoned near the monument, an unfortunate testament to the ruthless hostility of the rogue wizards occupying the island.",["al"]={"henze faulk body","who is the dead guy on the island"},["q"]="Who is Henze Faulk?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","henze faulk","heroes vigil","heroes' vigil","rogue wizards","stone cairn lake","stone of remembrance"},["n"]="Heroes' Vigil",["s"]="Heroes' Vigil is a quiet, sacred clearing situated on the central island within Stone Cairn Lake in eastern Elwynn Forest. Centered around a monument known as the Stone of Remembrance, it was dedicated to honor those who fell during the First War. Today, however, the shrine sits largely neglected by Stormwind and is overrun by dangerous renegade wizards.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Erected after the First War, Heroes' Vigil centers upon the Stone of Remembrance, an inscribed stone circle meant to honor the soldiers and citizens slaughtered during the Old Horde's sacking of Goldshire and the surrounding valleys. Though once revered as a sacred bastion of faith and sacrifice, the vigil has gradually slipped from the attention of Stormwind's current rulers, leaving its hallowed grounds overgrown and unattended by the realm's soldiers.",["t"]="A Forgotten Memorial"},{["b"]="Because the kingdom has left the island garrisoned by none, outcasts have seized the memorial. A cabal of rogue wizards now controls Stone Cairn Lake and the monument grounds, practicing wild and undisciplined magic away from the oversight of the Kirin Tor and the Academy of Arcane Sciences. The desecration is made all the more bitter by tragic casualties left near the stones, including the body of Henze Faulk, leaving travelers to wonder if the shrine will ever be restored to peace.",["t"]="Claimed by Renegades"}}}}}
t["subzone:hidden-path"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,276,15.419.0,23.422.0,32.217.0,38.238.0,65.250.0,42.174.0",["h"]="689a5a",["n"]="Sendero Oculto",["s"]="Sendero Oculto. El Sendero Oculto es un apartado camino de montaña que serpentea entre los riscos sobre el Valle de los Retos, en Durotar. Sirve como rito de iniciación para los aspirantes a chamán que buscan la sagrada Roca de los Espíritus, al tiempo que ofrece un mirador poco frecuentado que domina las escarpadas fronteras de Los Baldíos. Esculpido en los picos rojizos que bordean el Valle de los Retos, el Sendero Oculto es deliberadamente difícil de detectar desde el fondo del cañón. Los mentores guían a los jóvenes chamanes hasta aquí para poner a prueba su percepción y disciplina antes de comulgar con los espíritus en la Roca de los Espíritus. En los tramos más altos del sendero, los viajeros disfrutan de amplias vistas panorámicas que se extienden hacia el oeste, en dirección a las onduladas sabanas de Los Baldíos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="The Hidden Path is your first true physical and spiritual climb, testing your perception before you commune with the earth spirits at Spirit Rock.",["faction:Horde"]="Though sacred to shaman, this unfortified passage represents a security blind spot above the Valley of Trials that warrants a watchful eye."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The path ascends from the Valley of Trials up into the crags to Spirit Rock, a sacred site where shaman commune with the elements. It also winds along mountain passes that connect toward the Barrens and the coastline.",["al"]={"hidden path destination","where does hidden path go","hidden path leads to"},["q"]="Where does the Hidden Path lead?"},{["a"]="Initiate shaman in the Valley of Trials are tasked with locating this secluded trail as part of their early elemental trials. Climbing the path allows them to reach the Spirit Rock and drink the Sapta required to commune with the spirits.",["al"]={"shaman path valley of trials","spirit rock path","shaman quest path"},["q"]="Why is the path significant to shaman?"},{["a"]="Yes. The low gaps along the path bypass the standard guarded entrances to the valley. A cunning Alliance strike force coming from Ratchet or the coast could theoretically use the trail to bypass Horde scouts and enter the training grounds undetected.",["al"]={"hidden path alliance invasion","is valley of trials vulnerable","valley of trials back door"},["q"]="Could enemies use the Hidden Path to attack the Valley of Trials?"},{["a"]="At its highest point, the trail offers a clear, elevated view looking west toward the vast plains of the Barrens, as well as sweeping views across the red canyons of Durotar.",["al"]={"hidden path view","lookout point hidden path"},["q"]="What can you see from the top of the path?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","durotar","hidden path","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},["n"]="Hidden Path",["s"]="The Hidden Path is a secluded mountain trail winding through the crags above the Valley of Trials in Durotar. It serves as a rite of passage for aspiring shaman seeking the sacred Spirit Rock, while offering an overlooked vantage overlooking the rugged borders of the Barrens.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the red peaks bordering the Valley of Trials, the Hidden Path is intentionally difficult to spot from the canyon floor. Young shaman are directed here by their mentors to prove their awareness and discipline before communing with the spirits at Spirit Rock. Along the trail's highest reaches, travelers are treated to expansive panoramic views stretching westward toward the rolling savannas of the Barrens.",["t"]="A Sacred Ascent"},{["b"]="Beyond its spiritual importance, the path cuts a precarious breach through the natural fortifications enclosing the valley. A low pass along the route provides a direct back door toward Ratchet and the road to Orgrimmar. Because it circumvents the standard canyon checkpoints, vigilant defenders fear that bold Alliance infiltrators could exploit this quiet trail to slip directly into the Horde's primary proving grounds.",["t"]="Strategic Vulnerability"}}}}}
t["subzone:high-rise"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,350,18.713.0,31.224.0,41.258.0,51.248.0",["h"]="b04153",["n"]="Alto Superior",["s"]="Alto Superior. Alto Superior es el nivel superior de la meseta central de Cima del Trueno, coronando la capital de los tauren. Alberga un bullicioso anfiteatro centrado alrededor de una hoguera comunal junto a avezados artesanos, comerciantes de armas y maestros culinarios. A diferencia de los niveles inferiores, esta cumbre depende por completo de puentes colgantes de cuerda y del nido de jinetes del viento para viajar. Alto Superior se alza en lo alto de la meseta central de Cima del Trueno, recibiendo los vientos abiertos muy por encima de las Llanuras Onduladas de Mulgore. Punto de encuentro neurálgico para las tribus unidas, se articula en torno a un anfiteatro al aire libre y una hoguera donde los ciudadanos escuchan importantes anuncios tribales y decisiones trascendentales. Las tiendas y puestos de madera circundantes albergan a renombrados mercaderes, armerías e instructores culinarios, entre ellos la Cocina de Aska y el establecimiento Cebos y Aparejos de la Cumbre. Mientras que los niveles inferiores conectan directamente con la pradera de Mulgore mediante enormes ascensores de madera, el Alto Superior se mantiene en las alturas, accesible principalmente a través del nido de jinetes del viento y de amplios puentes de cuerda que lo unen con los altos vecinos: el Alto de los Ancestros y el Alto de los Cazadores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Cooking"]="The High Rise is home to Aska's Kitchen and renowned pit masters, making it the primary destination in Thunder Bluff to hone your culinary skills over open flame.",["race:Tauren"]="As the crest of your capital city, the High Rise represents unity among the tribes, gathering hunters, shamans, and elders around its high communal fire."},["faq"]={{["a"]="You can reach the High Rise through the central wind rider roost from the lower tiers, or across the suspension bridges from Elder Rise and Hunter Rise. There is no lift running directly from the Mulgore plains to this tier.",["al"]={"how to get to high rise","high rise access","getting up to high rise"},["q"]="How do you reach the High Rise?"},{["a"]="The tier is known for its tradesfolk and outdoor gathering places. Notable establishments include Aska's Kitchen for cooking instruction, Mountaintop Bait & Tackle for fishing gear, and various weapon merchants like Ragetotem Arms and Thunderhoof's Firearms.",["al"]={"trainers on high rise","shops high rise","what is on high rise"},["q"]="What services are found on the High Rise?"},{["a"]="The open-air amphitheater surrounds a central bonfire, serving as a communal gathering area. Here, the tauren people assemble beneath the open sky to hear news, deliberate tribal affairs, and witness important proclamations delivered atop the mesa.",["al"]={"high rise bonfire","high rise auditorium","tauren meeting place"},["q"]="What is the amphitheater on the High Rise used for?"}},["kw"]={"amphitheater","aska's kitchen","bonfire","high rise","mulgore","thunder bluff","wind rider roost"},["n"]="High Rise",["s"]="The High Rise is the uppermost tier of Thunder Bluff's central mesa, crowning the tauren capital. It hosts a bustling amphitheater centered around a communal bonfire alongside seasoned artisans, weapon merchants, and culinary masters. Unlike the lower tiers, this summit relies entirely on suspension rope bridges and the wind rider roost for travel.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The High Rise perches atop Thunder Bluff's core plateau, catching the open winds high above the rolling plains of Mulgore. A focal gathering point for the united tribes, it centers around an open-air amphitheater and fire pit where citizens listen to important tribal announcements and fateful decisions. The surrounding tents and wooden stalls house renowned merchants, armories, and culinary trainers, including Aska's Kitchen and Mountaintop Bait & Tackle. While the lower tiers connect directly to Mulgore's prairie floor via massive wooden elevators, the High Rise stays aloft, accessible primarily through the wind rider roost and sweeping rope bridges linking to the neighboring Elder Rise and Hunter Rise.",["t"]="Summit of the Mesa"}}}}}
t["subzone:high-seat"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,328,21.515.0,24.426.0,29.218.0,44.179.0,59.205.0,45.184.0",["h"]="a448f2",["n"]="Trono",["s"]="Trono. El Trono es la gran sala del trono de Forjaz, situada entre Distrito Comercial y la Gran Fundición. Desde esta cámara elevada, el Rey Magni Barbabronce preside el reino enano junto a sus consejeros reales e historiadores. La sala también alberga el pasadizo sellado que desciende a las antiguas profundidades de Viejo Forjaz. Con vistas a los bulliciosos anillos de Forjaz, el Trono sirve como la sede real del poder para el reino de Khaz Modan. Dentro de esta cámara abovedada, el Rey Magni Barbabronce atiende a los peticionarios, celebra consejos con sus asesores y dirige la defensa de los baluartes del norte de la Alianza. Flanqueado por dignatarios reales como el Historiador Real Archesonus y el Senador Barin Rocaroja, el Trono sigue siendo un símbolo de la inquebrantable autoridad Barbabronce y de la resistencia enana en tiempos turbulentos en todo Azeroth.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="As the seat of dwarven power, this chamber is critical to Alliance logistics and high-level strategy, housing envoys, advisors, and royal decrees.",["race:Dwarf"]="The High Seat represents the unbroken lineage of Khaz Modan's sovereignty, where King Magni Bronzebeard continues to lead his people with an iron will."},["faq"]={{["a"]="King Magni Bronzebeard rules Ironforge from the throne within the High Seat. He directs the affairs of the Bronzebeard clan, listens to subjects, and coordinates military and diplomatic matters with the Grand Alliance.",["al"]={"who is on the throne","ironforge king","magni throne room"},["q"]="Who rules from the High Seat?"},{["a"]="The chamber is centrally located in Ironforge, connected directly to the outer ring between the Commons and the Great Forge, allowing easy access for visiting citizens and envoys.",["al"]={"where is high seat","find high seat","throne room location"},["q"]="Where is the High Seat located in Ironforge?"},{["a"]="The large archway at the rear of the High Seat leads into Old Ironforge, the cavernous ancestral ruins that lie directly beneath the modern mountain city. Access to these lower passages remains restricted.",["al"]={"door behind magni","old ironforge door","high seat basement"},["q"]="What is the sealed corridor at the back of the throne room?"},{["a"]="King Magni is attended by prominent dwarven figures, including Royal Historian Archesonus, who safeguards the records and relics of the Bronzebeard dynasty, and Senator Barin Redstone.",["al"]={"high seat npcs","magni advisors"},["q"]="Who else can be found advising the King here?"}},["kw"]={"archesonus","barin redstone","bronzebeard","high seat","ironforge","magni","throne"},["n"]="High Seat",["s"]="The High Seat is the grand throne room of Ironforge, situated between the Commons and the Great Forge. From this elevated chamber, King Magni Bronzebeard presides over the dwarven realm alongside his royal advisors and historians. The room also houses the sealed passageway leading down into the ancient depths of Old Ironforge.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking the vibrant bustling rings of Ironforge, the High Seat serves as the royal seat of power for the kingdom of Khaz Modan. Within this vaulted chamber, King Magni Bronzebeard hears petitioners, holds council with his advisors, and directs the defense of the Alliance's northern bastions. Flanked by royal dignitaries such as Royal Historian Archesonus and Senator Barin Redstone, the High Seat remains a symbol of unyielding Bronzebeard authority and dwarven resilience amid troubling times across Azeroth.",["t"]="Heart of Dwarven Rule"},{["b"]="Behind the majestic stone appointments of the throne room lies a heavy doorway leading into the shadowy expanse of Old Ironforge. These lower ruins represent the original, ancestral halls carved out by the dwarves before the city was reconfigured around the Great Forge. Guarded and sealed to general traffic, the portal reminds visitors of the vast antiquity and cavernous history resting beneath the modern capital's stones.",["t"]="Gateway to Old Ironforge"}}}}}
t["subzone:hillsbrad-fields"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,358,30.630.0,32.592.0,47.312.0,35.283.0,41.315.0,49.299.0",["h"]="90a598",["n"]="Campos de Trabalomas",["s"]="Campos de Trabalomas. Los Campos de Trabalomas comprenden las tierras de cultivo y el asentamiento rústico de Trabalomas, en el oeste de Laderas de Trabalomas. Al ser una de las pocas comunidades humanas supervivientes de la antigua Lordaeron que se negó a sucumbir ante la Plaga o a unirse a la fanática Cruzada Escarlata, sus granjeros y su milicia se enfrentan ahora a constantes asaltos por parte de los Renegados del cercano Molino Tarren. Abarcando huertos, campos de calabazas y pastos entre Colinas de Darrow y la Mina Azur, los Campos de Trabalomas suministran provisiones esenciales a Costasur y a la resistencia superviviente de la Alianza. Mientras que gran parte de Lordaeron cayó ante la plaga de la no-muerte, la gente de Trabalomas resistió, conservando con orgullo el tabardo real y la heráldica de su reino caído. Liderado por el magistrado Burnside y el Consejo de Trabalomas, el municipio opera como un cuerpo cívico independiente bajo asedio constante. El herrero local Verringtan y sus aprendices mantienen armado al pueblo, asegurándose de que cada granjero y trabajador esté preparado para defender su tierra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Hillsbrad Fields are a vital breadbasket and a poignant symbol of Lordaeron's enduring spirit, warranting protection against Forsaken extermination.",["faction:Horde"]="High Executor Darthalia demands the systematic dismantling of Hillsbrad's farms and militia to secure the southern frontier for the Forsaken."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Hillsbrad and neighbouring Southshore are among the very few settlements in Lordaeron that avoided complete destruction by the Scourge during the Third War. Unlike other survivors who fled south or joined the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, these residents remained to rebuild their lives and maintain their homeland.",["al"]={"why are humans in hillsbrad","who lives in hillsbrad fields","are the farmers alive"},["q"]="Why are there still living humans farming here?"},{["a"]="The town and farmlands are governed by Magistrate Burnside, aided by Clerk Horrace Whitesteed and the Council of Hillsbrad from the local town hall. Landowners such as Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz manage the surrounding estates, while local blacksmith Verringtan equips the town watch.",["al"]={"who leads hillsbrad","hillsbrad leadership","magistrate of hillsbrad"},["q"]="Who rules over the town and fields?"},{["a"]="High Executor Darthalia at Tarren Mill considers Hillsbrad a dangerous Alliance foothold on the Forsaken border. Undercity orders direct soldiers to break the human supply lines by destroying food stores, slaughtering livestock, and eliminating town leaders to clear the way for Forsaken dominance in the foothills.",["al"]={"why forsaken attack hillsbrad","battle of hillsbrad reason","tarren mill attacks"},["q"]="Why are the Forsaken attacking the farms?"},{["a"]="During the Second War, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer ordered a devastating assault on Hillsbrad to break human morale while building up Horde forces in the Southshore region. Hillsbrad was destroyed in a gruesome show of force, but the Alliance drove the orcs out and the town was subsequently rebuilt.",["al"]={"hillsbrad second war","orcs destroyed hillsbrad","history of hillsbrad fields"},["q"]="What happened to Hillsbrad during the Second War?"}},["kw"]={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","farmer getz","farmer ray","hillsbrad","hillsbrad fields","magistrate burnside","southshore","tarren mill","verringtan"},["n"]="Hillsbrad Fields",["s"]="The Hillsbrad Fields encompass the cultivated farmlands and rustic settlement of Hillsbrad in western Hillsbrad Foothills. As one of the few surviving human communities in former Lordaeron that refused to succumb to the Scourge or join the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, its farmers and militia now face constant assaults from the nearby Forsaken at Tarren Mill.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning orchards, pumpkin patches, and pastures between Darrow Hill and the Azurelode Mine, the Hillsbrad Fields supply essential provisions to Southshore and the surviving Alliance resistance. While much of Lordaeron fell to the plague of undeath, the people of Hillsbrad endured, proudly retaining the royal tabard and heraldry of their fallen kingdom. Led by Magistrate Burnside and the Council of Hillsbrad, the township operates as an independent civic body under constant siege. The local blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices keep the populace armed, ensuring every farmer and laborer is prepared to defend their land.",["t"]="A Defiant Bastion of Lordaeron"},{["b"]="The fertile fields are a prime target for High Executor Darthalia and the Forsaken forces entrenched at Tarren Mill. Viewing the thriving human settlement as an existential threat on their southern flank, the Undercity has orchestrated continuous raids against the community's infrastructure, targeting crops, livestock, councilors, and civilian farmers alike. In response, Hillsbrad's defenders have formed a hardened militia. Far from helpless peasants, local landowners like Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz organize ambushes and fight fiercely against undead incursions to preserve their homes.",["t"]="Front Line of the Undead Advance"}}}}}
t["subzone:hunter-rise"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,329,23.447.0,24.382.0,29.178.0,36.217.0,26.218.0,46.203.0",["h"]="2ea011",["n"]="Alto de los Cazadores",["s"]="Alto de los Cazadores. El Alto de los Cazadores es una de las mesetas elevadas que componen la ciudad de Cima del Trueno, situada justo al sur del risco central. Sirve como el principal punto de entrenamiento y reunión para los guerreros, cazadores, rastreadores y desolladores tauren. A lo largo de sus plataformas azotadas por el viento, los jóvenes bravos perfeccionan sus habilidades marciales y se preparan para el combate. Conectado a los riscos vecinos mediante puentes de cuerda colgantes, el Alto de los Cazadores está dedicado a las tradiciones marciales de los tauren. Su núcleo es la Sala de los Cazadores, donde tiradores, rastreadores y guerreros experimentados transmiten su disciplina a las generaciones más jóvenes. Alrededor del pabellón hay campos de prácticas equipados con maniquíes de entrenamiento, armeros y postes de desuello, lo que lo convierte en un bullicioso centro para aquellos que viven de la lanza, el arco y el pellejo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="For young tauren hunters, this rise is the natural heart of your calling in the capital, providing training, pet supplies, and guidance from master trackers.",["class:Warrior"]="The grounds of Hunter Rise provide training dummies, combat mentors, and battlemasters eager to test your strength in the ongoing defense of the Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Hunter Rise is located on the southern side of Thunder Bluff. It is reached by crossing the wooden rope bridges that connect it to the lower rise and high rise mesas of the city.",["al"]={"where is hunter rise","hunter rise location","how to get to hunter rise"},["q"]="Where is Hunter Rise located?"},{["a"]="The mesa is home to tauren hunters, warriors, trackers, trappers, and leatherworkers. In addition to class and profession trainers, Horde battlemasters make their stand here to recruit fighters for the faction's wars.",["al"]={"who is on hunter rise","hunter rise trainers","what is on hunter rise"},["q"]="Who lives and trains on Hunter Rise?"},{["a"]="The Hunter's Hall is the primary longhouse on the rise where seasoned hunters and warriors congregate. It serves as an armory, school, and hearth for those learning the ways of tracking, marksmanship, and close combat.",["al"]={"hunters hall","hunters lodge thunder bluff","thunder bluff hunter hall"},["q"]="What is the Hunter's Hall?"},{["a"]="No. Thunder Bluff is a major Horde capital city, and Hunter Rise is guarded by seasoned tauren braves. Any Alliance adventurer attempting to cross its bridges will be attacked immediately by city guards.",["al"]={"alliance on hunter rise","can alliance go to hunter rise"},["q"]="Can members of the Alliance visit Hunter Rise?"}},["kw"]={"battlemasters","hunter rise","hunter's hall","mulgore","thunder bluff","trackers"},["n"]="Hunter Rise",["s"]="Hunter Rise is one of the elevated mesas making up the city of Thunder Bluff, situated just south of the central bluff. It serves as the primary training and gathering ground for the tauren's warriors, hunters, trackers, and skinners. Across its windswept platforms, young braves hone their martial skills and prepare for combat.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Connected to the neighboring bluffs by swaying rope bridges, Hunter Rise is dedicated to the martial traditions of the tauren. It is anchored by the Hunter's Hall, where experienced marksmen, trackers, and warriors pass down their discipline to younger generations. Surrounding the lodge are practice grounds outfitted with training dummies, weapon racks, and skinning posts, making it a bustling center for those who live by spear, bow, and hide.",["t"]="The Gathering of Braves"},{["b"]="Beyond hunting wild game across the plains of Mulgore, the inhabitants of Hunter Rise help ensure the defense of Thunder Bluff and the wider Horde. Battlemasters stationed along the rise recruit seasoned fighters to answer the call of skirmishes against Alliance incursions across contested battlegrounds. It remains an essential rallying point for anyone sworn to protect the herd.",["t"]="Martial Duty and Defense"}}}}}
t["subzone:hushed-bank"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,301,26.442.0,20.405.1,33.232.0,42.177.0,32.190.0,44.166.0",["h"]="5acd6c",["n"]="La Ribera Silente",["s"]="La Ribera Silente. La Ribera Silente es la sombría costa occidental de Bosque del Ocaso, que bordea el río que separa el bosque de Páramos de Poniente. Extendiéndose desde el cruce cerca de Tres Caminos hacia el sur en dirección a Vega de Tuercespina, es un bosque silencioso pero peligroso acechado por bestias merodeadoras y ensombrecido por oscuros misterios. Extendiéndose a lo largo del límite fluvial entre Bosque del Ocaso y Páramos de Poniente, La Ribera Silente marca la transición de las llanuras abiertas y las granjas soleadas al crepúsculo omnipresente y antinatural. El puente cubierto de madera cruza el río aquí, ofreciendo paso a los viajeros que se dirigen al oeste fuera del lúgubre bosque. La densa maleza y la niebla que se arrastra dominan las orillas del río, donde grandes arañas y hambrientos lobos del bosque acechan a los caminantes incautos que se desvían del camino transitado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The wolves and spiders haunting the dense foliage along the riverbank offer classic wilderness beasts for trackers charting the darker reaches of the forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="The covered bridge along the bank serves as a critical strategic passage connecting the farmlands of Westfall to the besieged outpost of Duskwood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Hushed Bank forms the western edge of Duskwood along the river that separates the forest from Westfall. It extends from the fork near Three Corners in the north down toward the southern borders leading toward Stranglethorn Vale.",["al"]={"hushed bank location","where is hushed bank","hushed bank map"},["q"]="Where is the Hushed Bank located?"},{["a"]="A wooden covered bridge spans the river at the Hushed Bank, allowing foot and cart traffic to cross safely between the sunny plains of Westfall and the cursed gloom of Duskwood.",["al"]={"bridge to westfall","westfall bridge duskwood","how to cross river to westfall"},["q"]="What connects the Hushed Bank to Westfall?"},{["a"]="Sven Yorgen and his associate Lars have established an encampment in the northern corner of the bank. Both live as isolated recluses, having fled the horrors that claimed Sven's nearby farm.",["al"]={"camp on hushed bank","who is at hushed bank","npcs hushed bank"},["q"]="Who lives along the Hushed Bank?"},{["a"]="The Hushed Bank is home to vicious woodland beasts, including overgrown webwood spiders and predatory dusking wolves that prey upon anything moving through the brush.",["al"]={"hushed bank mobs","dangers of hushed bank","hushed bank monsters"},["q"]="What threats are found along this shoreline?"}},["kw"]={"covered bridge","duskwood","hushed bank","lars","riverbank","sven yorgen","westfall"},["n"]="Hushed Bank",["s"]="The Hushed Bank is the shadowy western shoreline of Duskwood, bordering the river that divides the forest from Westfall. Stretching from the junction near the Three Corners south toward Stranglethorn Vale, it is a quiet yet hazardous woodland stalked by prowling beasts and shadowed by dark mysteries.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running along the river boundary between Duskwood and Westfall, the Hushed Bank marks the transition from open plains and sunlit farms to pervasive, unnatural twilight. The wooden covered bridge crosses the river here, offering passage to travelers heading west out of the grim wood. Thick underbrush and creeping fog dominate the riverbanks, where large spiders and hungry forest wolves stalk unwary wayfarers who stray from the beaten path.",["t"]="A Frontier Along the River"},{["b"]="Near the northern reaches of the bank, solitary souls have carved out meager existences away from the suspicious eyes of Darkshire. Sven Yorgen and his companion Lars keep camp in these dense woods, watching the treeline and harboring bitter grievances tied to the dark tragedies that plagued the region. Their isolated refuge remains one of the few signs of living humanoid presence on this lonely shore.",["t"]="Outcasts and Hermits"}}}}}
t["subzone:iris-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,251,16.450.0,20.376.0,46.237.0,37.183.0,23.211.0,27.149.0",["h"]="fd9bb2",["n"]="Lago Iris",["s"]="Lago Iris. El Lago Iris es una masa de agua marchita situada en la parte central norte de Vallefresno, al este de Astranaar. Antaño cristalinas, sus aguas se han vuelto de un color verde amarillento enfermizo debido a la corrupción demoníaca que se filtra desde Frondavil, y ahora hostiles bestias del pantano merodean por sus orillas. Enclavado entre Astranaar y la poza de la luna custodiada por Shael'dryn, el Lago Iris se erige como un sombrío recordatorio de las heridas infligidas durante la Tercera Guerra. Las energías viles que bajan hacia el sur desde las contaminadas alturas de Frondavil han envenenado la cuenca, convirtiendo sus otrora claras aguas en un cenagal fétido y de un verde amarillento enfermizo. La corrupción ha retorcido la vegetación autóctona y los espíritus del agua, haciendo surgir agresivas bestias del pantano que atacan a cualquier viajero que se acerque.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The twisted bog beasts and stagnant, corrupted waters demonstrate the devastating toll that demonic energy takes on nature when left unchecked.",["race:NightElf"]="Iris Lake is a heartbreaking example of the creeping corruption threatening Ashenvale, but recovering Elune's Tears from its fouled shores offers hope for cleansing the forest."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Iris Lake has been tainted by demonic corruption bleeding down from neighboring Felwood. The dark magic has poisoned the water table, turning the lake into a yellowish-green pool that twists nearby wildlife into aggressive monstrosities.",["al"]={"why is iris lake green","iris lake water","why is iris lake tainted"},["q"]="Why is the water at Iris Lake green and murky?"},{["a"]="The lake and its shores are infested with corrupted bog beasts. These plant and mud elementals have been maddened by fel energy and will violently attack anyone approaching the water.",["al"]={"iris lake monsters","iris lake mobs","what attacks at iris lake"},["q"]="What creatures roam around Iris Lake?"},{["a"]="Elune's Tears are sacred glowing blue stones found near the shores of Iris Lake. Priests and keepers of the night elves use their consecrated nature in purification rites, notably to cleanse corrupted moonwells.",["al"]={"elunes tears","elune tear","what is elunes tear"},["q"]="What are Elune's Tears?"},{["a"]="Iris Lake lies in north-central Ashenvale. It is positioned directly east of the night elf settlement of Astranaar and west of Shael'dryn's moonwell.",["al"]={"where is iris lake","iris lake location","how to get to iris lake"},["q"]="Where is Iris Lake located?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","bog beasts","elune's tear","felwood corruption","iris lake","shael'dryn"},["n"]="Iris Lake",["s"]="Iris Lake is a blighted body of water resting in north-central Ashenvale, east of Astranaar. Once pristine, its waters have turned a sickly yellowish-green from demonic corruption seeping down from Felwood, and hostile bog beasts now prowl its shores.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled between Astranaar and the moonwell tended by Shael'dryn, Iris Lake stands as a grim reminder of the wounds inflicted during the Third War. Fel energies drifting south from the tainted heights of Felwood have poisoned the basin, turning its once-clear waters into a foul, sickly yellow-green mire. The corruption has twisted the native plant life and water spirits, raising aggressive bog beasts that lash out at any traveler who wanders near.",["t"]="A Tainted Refuge"},{["b"]="Despite the severe pollution choking the lake, sacred remnants of the past still linger along its edges. Rare crystalline stones known as Elune's Tears can sometimes be found resting along the muddy banks. Keepers of elven traditions, such as Shael'dryn, seek these holy stones to aid in purifying tainted moonwells and resisting the spreading demonic blight across Ashenvale.",["t"]="Tears of the Goddess"}}}}}
t["subzone:ironband-s-compound"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,261,24.428.0,21.297.0,41.128.0,37.133.0,37.96.0,55.201.0",["h"]="005b1d",["n"]="Complejo Vetaferro",["s"]="Complejo Vetaferro. El Complejo Vetaferro es un puesto fortificado enclavado en las colinas nevadas al sur del Lago de Helm, en la zona oriental de Dun Morogh. Anteriormente hogar del prospector Sturgy Ironband, el campamento ha sido invadido por hostiles enanos Hierro Negro que atacan a cualquiera que se acerque demasiado. Establecido originalmente por Sturgy Ironband, este complejo al sur del Lago de Helm sirvió antaño como base de operaciones en los parajes nevados de Dun Morogh. Todo cambió cuando los infiltrados Hierro Negro se adentraron en territorio Barbabronce y se apoderaron del lugar. Ahora, repleto de enanos hostiles, el complejo funciona como una base avanzada enemiga que amenaza a viajeros y asentamientos cercanos, justo ante las narices de Forjaz.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Aspiring warriors are dispatched here by Ironforge's veteran trainers to prove their mettle by aiding fallen comrades and collecting proof of the Dark Iron presence.",["race:Dwarf"]="For the Bronzebeards, seeing the treacherous Dark Irons entrenching themselves within Dun Morogh's borders is a direct insult and a persistent danger to their homeland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The outpost was formerly inhabited and used by Sturgy Ironband before hostile forces drove him out and took control of the site.",["al"]={"who made this camp","sturgy ironband","who owns ironbands compound"},["q"]="Who originally built Ironband's Compound?"},{["a"]="The camp has been seized by a band of hostile Dark Iron dwarves who readily assault any wanderers or Ironforge patrols that approach.",["al"]={"who is here","what enemies are here","dark irons dun morogh"},["q"]="Who controls Ironband's Compound now?"},{["a"]="You can find it nestled in the snowy hills of eastern Dun Morogh, just south of Helm's Bed Lake.",["al"]={"where is ironbands compound","how to find ironband compound","ironband location"},["q"]="Where is Ironband's Compound located?"},{["a"]="Having an enemy clan establish a fortified base so close to the dwarf capital is an alarming security breach. Ironforge authorities send fighters here to gather hard evidence of Dark Iron infiltration.",["al"]={"why care about this camp","ironforge response","dark iron threat"},["q"]="Why is this camp important to the leaders of Ironforge?"}},["kw"]={"dark iron","dun morogh","dwarf","helm's bed lake","ironband's compound","ironforge","sturgy ironband"},["n"]="Ironband's Compound",["s"]="Ironband's Compound is a fortified outpost tucked into the snowy hills south of Helm's Bed Lake in eastern Dun Morogh. Formerly home to the prospector Sturgy Ironband, the camp has been overrun by hostile Dark Iron dwarves who attack anyone venturing too close.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Originally established by Sturgy Ironband, this compound south of Helm's Bed Lake once served as a staging post in the snowy wilderness of Dun Morogh. That changed when Dark Iron infiltrators pushed deep into Bronzebeard territory and seized the site for themselves. Now bristling with hostile dwarves, the compound serves as an enemy forward base threatening travelers and nearby settlements, right under the nose of Ironforge.",["t"]="A Fall to the Dark Irons"},{["b"]="The presence of a fortified Dark Iron camp within Dun Morogh's own borders is a serious provocation. Ironforge keeps a wary eye on the compound, dispatching seasoned warriors to recover fallen scouts and secure vital intelligence proving the extent of the Dark Iron threat in the mountain kingdom.",["t"]="A Threat to Ironforge"}}}}}
t["subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="26,280,19.480.0,22.380.0,44.134.0,27.187.0,47.223.0,42.191.0",["h"]="1571a0",["n"]="Excavación de Vetaferro",["s"]="Excavación de Vetaferro. La Excavación de Vetaferro es una amplia excavación enana situada en el sureste de Loch Modan, justo al sur del lago y al suroeste de la Cabaña del Errante. Dirigida por el Prospector Vetaferro, la operación arqueológica se detuvo bruscamente cuando unos troggs agresivos e inestables invadieron las trincheras. Impulsado por el afán de los enanos por descubrir sus antiguos orígenes titánicos, el Prospector Vetaferro estableció esta vasta excavación junto a los escarpados acantilados del sureste de Loch Modan. Lo que comenzó como una excavación prometedora se convirtió rápidamente en un desastre cuando las obras perturbaron a una raza subterránea de troggs inusualmente feroces y corpulentos. Las criaturas surgieron de la tierra, haciendo retroceder a los mineros y acampando entre herramientas dispersas, carretas rotas y reliquias a medio desenterrar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Mining"]="The quarry and open pits showcase typical dwarven heavy-extraction techniques, though ongoing trogg hostility makes any prospecting hazardous.",["race:Dwarf"]="The overrun dig is a stinging setback for the Explorers' League, who view the recovery of ancient relics here as vital to understanding dwarven heritage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The excavation site is located in the southeastern region of Loch Modan, directly south of the Loch and southwest of Farstrider Lodge.",["al"]={"ironband location","where is ironbands digsite","ironband map"},["q"]="Where is Ironband's Excavation Site located?"},{["a"]="Prospector Ironband is an archaeologist and explorer heading up the excavation on behalf of the dwarven Explorers' League, attempting to salvage artifacts and drive back the local troggs.",["al"]={"who is ironband","prospector ironband lore"},["q"]="Who is Prospector Ironband?"},{["a"]="As the dwarven miners excavated deeper into the soil of Loch Modan, their tunneling breached subterranean pockets inhabited by a large and aggressive breed of troggs, who quickly overwhelmed the workers and seized the site.",["al"]={"why are troggs here","who attacked the digsite","ironband troggs"},["q"]="Why is the excavation site overrun with troggs?"},{["a"]="Like many dwarven archaeological digs across Khaz Modan, the miners were searching for ancient Titan relics and stone ruins that might shed light on the ancestral origins of the dwarven race.",["al"]={"what are they digging for","ironband artifacts","why dig here"},["q"]="What were the dwarves hoping to find here?"}},["kw"]={"digsite","excavation site","explorers league","ironband","loch modan","prospector ironband","troggs"},["n"]="Ironband's Excavation Site",["s"]="Ironband's Excavation Site is an expansive dwarven dig located in southeastern Loch Modan, just south of the lake and southwest of Farstrider Lodge. Led by Prospector Ironband, the archaeological operation was abruptly halted when aggressive, volatile troggs overran the trenches.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spurred by the dwarven drive to uncover their ancient Titan origins, Prospector Ironband established this sprawling digsite along the rugged cliffs of southeastern Loch Modan. What began as a promising excavation quickly turned into a disaster when the digging disturbed an unusually fierce and large breed of subterranean troggs. The creatures surged from the earth, driving back the miners and setting up camp amidst the scattered tools, broken carts, and half-excavated relics.",["t"]="Unearthing the Past"},{["b"]="Much like archaeological efforts in the Badlands, Wetlands, and Uldaman, the site sits in dangerous limbo. Surviving prospectors cling to the edges of the perimeter, desperate to reclaim their stolen gear and protect exposed artifacts—including strange ancient statues left behind by long-forgotten builders—from being smashed or carried off by the ravenous trogg infestation.",["t"]="Ruins in the Red Earth"}}}}}
t["subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,359,24.600.0,18.241.0,26.196.0,44.153.0,34.143.0",["h"]="75acd9",["n"]="Tumba de Barbaférrea",["s"]="Tumba de Barbaférrea. La Tumba de Barbaférrea es un lugar de enterramiento enano profanado situado al oeste del camino que conduce al norte hacia Dun Modr, en Los Humedales. Marcada por un cementerio al aire libre y una estatua de piedra que le da nombre, la cripta ha caído en desuso a medida que los mocos ácidos invadían el terreno. Los viajeros rara vez ponen un pie en la hondonada a menos que busquen pertenencias perdidas devoradas por el fango. Con vistas a las marismas a lo largo del camino hacia el norte a Dun Modr, la Tumba de Barbaférrea se erige como testimonio de la presencia enana en Los Humedales. Una monumental estatua de piedra, que presumiblemente representa al propio Barbaférrea, vigila el cementerio circundante. Sin embargo, la solemne paz ya no vela este lugar. La cripta subterránea ha sido invadida por completo por cepas de mocos negros y carmesíes, dejando la tumba contaminada. Los enanos ya no traen a sus muertos a este santuario en ruinas, y los pocos valientes que se atreven a perturbar las bóvedas lo hacen principalmente para rebuscar entre los restos digeridos por los limos acechantes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a clan hero's final resting place infested by mindless marsh oozes is a bitter disgrace for any dwarf traveling the road toward the Thandol Span."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Very little is recorded about Ironbeard himself, though the massive statue and crypt grounds suggest he was an honored dwarven figure of note in the Wetlands. The monument erected in his likeness watches over the hillside above the cemetery.",["al"]={"ironbeard lore","who is ironbeard","statue identity"},["q"]="Who was Ironbeard?"},{["a"]="The crypt has been completely overrun by acidic black and crimson oozes. With the burial grounds defiled and infested with dangerous slimes, mourning families have ceased bringing their dead here.",["al"]={"why abandoned","oozes in tomb","what happened to the crypt"},["q"]="Why is the tomb abandoned?"},{["a"]="Beyond fighting back the foul infestation, travelers frequently search the tomb's slimes hoping to recover swallowed items, most notably Sida's lost bag.",["al"]={"why go here","sida bag","tomb quests"},["q"]="Why do adventurers explore Ironbeard's Tomb?"},{["a"]="The tomb sits in north-central Wetlands, nestled into the hill just west of the main road heading north toward the dwarven redoubt of Dun Modr.",["al"]={"tomb location","how to get to ironbeard tomb","ironbeard wetlands map"},["q"]="Where is Ironbeard's Tomb located?"}},["kw"]={"crypt","dun modr","graveyard","ironbeard","ironbeard's tomb","oozes","sida","wetlands"},["n"]="Ironbeard's Tomb",["s"]="Ironbeard's Tomb is a defiled dwarven burial site situated west of the road leading north toward Dun Modr in the Wetlands. Marked by an outdoor graveyard and a stone statue of its namesake, the crypt has fallen into disuse as acidic oozes swarm the grounds. Travelers rarely set foot in the hollow unless searching for lost possessions swallowed by the slime.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking the marshes along the road north to Dun Modr, Ironbeard's Tomb stands as a testament to the dwarven presence in the Wetlands. A monumental stone statue, presumed to depict Ironbeard himself, watches over the surrounding burial plot. Yet solemn peace no longer keeps vigil here. The subterranean crypt has been completely overrun by oozes of various black and crimson strains, leaving the tomb contaminated. Dwarves no longer bring their dead to this ruined sanctuary, and those brave enough to disturb the vaults do so primarily to hunt through the remains digested by the lurking slimes.",["t"]="A Befouled Resting Place"}}}}}
t["subzone:ironclad-cove"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,235,19.576.0,20.553.1,50.256.0,49.204.0,27.252.0,34.197.0",["h"]="bef923",["n"]="Cala del Acorazado",["s"]="Cala del Acorazado. La Cala del Acorazado es una inmensa caverna subterránea oculta bajo Páramos de Poniente que alberga un astillero y un muelle subterráneos. Sirve como dársena secreta de construcción para el gran acorazado de la Hermandad Defias y conecta directamente con el mar. Enterrada en el punto más profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte, la Cala del Acorazado es una monumental caverna marina convertida en un astillero fortificado. Aquí, Edwin VanCleef y la Hermandad Defias han construido un enorme buque de guerra conocido como el acorazado. La caverna cuenta con extensos andamios de madera, islotes y pasarelas de carga tripuladas por piratas Defias, marineros y capataces. Su existencia revela la verdadera magnitud de la amenaza Defias: VanCleef no solo pretende asaltar las granjas de Páramos de Poniente, sino reunir una fuerza naval privada capaz de bombardear las mismísimas costas de Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The cove represents the zenith of Edwin VanCleef's craftsmanship, engineering prowess, and underground logistics, making it legendary among thieves and outlaws.",["faction:Alliance"]="Finding a full-sized war galleon buried under Westfall transforms the Defias from a regional bandit gang into an existential military threat against the Kingdom of Stormwind."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The juggernaught is the centerpiece of Edwin VanCleef's military ambitions. The Defias Brotherhood assembled this massive warship deep beneath the earth so it could launch undetected through subterranean water channels and strike at Stormwind from the sea.",["al"]={"why is there a ship here","what is the juggernaught","deadmines ship purpose"},["q"]="What is the ship in Ironclad Cove being built for?"},{["a"]="The massive gates open directly into the ocean along the southern coast of Westfall, near the border of northern Stranglethorn Vale. When opened, the juggernaught can sail straight out into the Great Sea.",["al"]={"where do the sea gates open","deadmines iron doors","exit into the ocean"},["q"]="Where does the large metal door in the cove lead?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood holds the cove under the command of Edwin VanCleef. While independent pirates originally used the secluded cavern, VanCleef's forces wiped them out to commandeer the docks and keep the juggernaught's construction entirely secret.",["al"]={"who runs the cove","who lives in ironclad cove"},["q"]="Who controls Ironclad Cove?"},{["a"]="That is Cookie, the Defias ship's cook. Armed with a rolling pin and cooking cauldrons, he is an unusual ally among the human and goblin renegades, having claimed the galley as his personal domain.",["al"]={"cookie the murloc","why is there a murloc pirate","chef cookie"},["q"]="Who is the murloc aboard the ship?"}},["kw"]={"cookie","deadmines ship","defias cove","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","shipyard"},["n"]="Ironclad Cove",["s"]="Ironclad Cove is a massive subterranean cavern hidden beneath Westfall, housing an underground shipyard and dock. It serves as the secret construction dock for the Defias Brotherhood's war juggernaught and connects directly to the sea.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Buried at the deepest point of the Deadmines, Ironclad Cove is a monumental sea cavern converted into a fortified dockyard. Here, Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood have constructed an enormous warship known as the juggernaught. The cavern features extensive wooden scaffolding, islets, and loading catwalks manned by Defias pirates, deckhands, and overseers. Its existence reveals the true scale of the Defias threat: VanCleef intends not merely to raid Westfall's farmsteads, but to assemble a private naval force capable of bombarding the shores of Stormwind itself.",["t"]="The Hidden Shipyard"},{["b"]="The cavern is dominated by colossal iron-reinforced sea doors set into the rock wall. Once opened, these gates provide a direct outlet into the Great Sea, emerging along the coastline just north of Stranglethorn Vale. Before the Defias Brotherhood seized the cove, it was held by an independent pirate crew whom the Brotherhood slaughtered to ensure total secrecy. Shielded from the eyes of the Stormwind naval fleet, the cove provides the Brotherhood an unmonitored lane for moving contraband, staging maritime raids, and preparing their naval assault.",["t"]="Gateway to the Ocean"}}}}}
t["subzone:ironforge-airfield"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,304,29.419.0,38.403.0,34.276.0,34.225.0,41.167.0,44.184.0",["h"]="288c7a",["n"]="Aeródromo de Forjaz",["s"]="Aeródromo de Forjaz. Escondida en lo alto de los picos nevados al noreste de Forjaz, esta remota pista de aterrizaje enana sirve como campo de pruebas y zona de operaciones para las máquinas voladoras de los gnomos y los montañeros enanos. Sin caminos principales que la señalen, la meseta se alza sobre los riscos escarpados de Dun Morogh y el pronunciado descenso hacia Los Humedales. Encaramado muy por encima de los senderos trillados de Dun Morogh, este aeródromo de gran altitud es una discreta maravilla de la cooperación de la Alianza. Al abrigo de las cumbres montañosas circundantes, la cantería enana afianza las crestas azotadas por el viento, mientras que las máquinas voladoras gnomo permanecen estacionadas a lo largo de pistas de aterrizaje al aire libre. Los montañeros vigilan el perímetro junto a ingenieros ocupados en ajustar engranajes e inspeccionar motores que escupen vapor en medio del frío cortante.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="For tinkers, the airstrip showcases the apex of gnomish aviation, featuring fully assembled flying machines stationed in extreme, sub-zero conditions.",["race:Dwarf"]="A testament to dwarven territorial watchfulness, the airfield proves that Ironforge's Mountaineers stand sentry even in the most inaccessible heights of Khaz Modan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="There are no roads, flights, or maintained tunnels connecting the valley to Ironforge or lower Dun Morogh. Reaching it requires scaling the steep mountainsides on foot, typically via tricky ridgeline climbing paths beginning out of Loch Modan or near the passes of Dun Morogh.",["al"]={"get to airfield","how to climb to airfield","airfield location","airfield path"},["q"]="How do you get up to the airfield?"},{["a"]="It serves as an elevated flight testing and military outpost where dwarven mountaineers and gnome engineers maintain flying machines and scout the high mountain borderlands separating Dun Morogh, Loch Modan, and the Wetlands.",["al"]={"why is there an airstrip","what is ironforge airfield for"},["q"]="What is the purpose of this place?"},{["a"]="Local Frostmane trolls inhabit caves in the southern cliffs of the valley. Dwarven mountaineers clash regularly with them over the frozen lake just beneath the runway.",["al"]={"who attacks airfield","who is fighting on the lake"},["q"]="Who is attacking the dwarven guards here?"},{["a"]="No standard quests direct adventurers to visit the airstrip in everyday travels. It remains an obscure, remote plateau largely separated from the main logistics of the dwarven kingdom.",["al"]={"any quests here","airfield quests"},["q"]="Is the airfield tied to any official quests?"}},["kw"]={"airfield","airstrip","dun morogh","flying machine","frostmane","ironforge","mountaineers"},["n"]="Ironforge Airfield",["s"]="Tucked away high in the snowy peaks northeast of Ironforge, this remote dwarven airstrip serves as a proving ground and staging area for gnome flying machines and dwarven mountaineers. Unmarked by main roads, the plateau overlooks the jagged crags of Dun Morogh and the steep descent toward the Wetlands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched far above the beaten trails of Dun Morogh, the high-altitude airfield is a quiet marvel of Alliance cooperation. Sheltered by surrounding mountain peaks, dwarven masonry anchors the blustery ridgelines while gnomish flying machines sit parked along open landing strips. Mountaineers keep watch over the perimeter alongside engineers busy wrenching gears and inspecting steam-belching engines in the biting cold.",["t"]="A Hidden Redoubt in the Crags"},{["b"]="Despite its isolation, the airfield is far from serene. The surrounding valley features frozen waters and crags contested by Frostmane trolls, who dwell in nearby caves and constantly harass the dwarven sentries. In the shadow of the peaks, dwarven defenders and Stormpike patrols clash regularly with troll raiders across the ice, keeping the remote installation in a state of quiet, vigilant standoff.",["t"]="Frontier Skirmishes and Frozen Valleys"}}}}}
t["subzone:ivar-patch"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,241,16.461.0,23.475.1,40.206.0,52.307.0,41.184.0,32.134.0",["h"]="c8c9b0",["n"]="Los Dominios de Ivar",["s"]="Los Dominios de Ivar. Los Dominios de Ivar son una granja de calabazas asolada ubicada en el norte del Bosque de Argénteos. En su día fue una próspera finca agrícola de Lordaeron, pero sus residentes fueron aniquilados durante la Tercera Guerra y transformados en necrófagos voraces y ciegamente hostiles. Antes de que la Tercera Guerra arrasara Lordaeron, este campo de calabazas era una próspera propiedad de un granjero llamado Ivar, quien empleaba a un animado grupo de peones y sirvientes. Cuando la Plaga desató la peste de la no-muerte por la campiña, la granja quedó completamente consumida. En lugar de alzarse con la mente intacta como los Renegados de libre albedrío, Ivar, su familia y sus trabajadores quedaron reducidos a necrófagos putrefactos y salvajes, condenados a merodear por la tierra en ruinas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Culling the ravenous ghouls at the patch is vital to securing the northern roadway between Silverpine Forest and the safety of Undercity.",["race:Undead"]="The ruined farm stands as a bitter reminder of the Plague of Undeath that tore Lordaeron apart, showing the horrifying mindless fate the Forsaken narrowly escaped."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farm was struck down by the Plague of Undeath during the Third War. Farmer Ivar, his family, and his workers all succumbed, rising again as feral, rotting ghouls under the lingering sway of the Scourge.",["al"]={"ivar patch history","who was ivar","what happened to ivar"},["q"]="What happened to the farm and its owner?"},{["a"]="Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick were part of a scouting reconnaissance squad dispatched to gauge regional threats in Silverpine Forest. While passing through, they were ambushed by the ghouls, and Quinn was severely injured by Ivar the Foul, forcing them to take refuge inside the dilapidated farmhouse.",["al"]={"deathstalkers at ivar patch","why are forsaken here","quinn yorick farmhouse"},["q"]="Why are there Deathstalkers hiding inside the house?"},{["a"]="No. The ghouls roaming the pumpkin fields are mindless Scourge remnants created by the Plague of Undeath. They lack free will and will attack any living travelers or Forsaken on sight.",["al"]={"are these ghouls forsaken","scourge in ivar patch","why are ghouls hostile"},["q"]="Are the ghouls here part of the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="The Ivar Patch lies in northern Silverpine Forest, north of the Dead Field and just south of the road leading toward Malden's Orchard.",["al"]={"ivar patch location","where is ivar patch"},["q"]="Where is the Ivar Patch located?"}},["kw"]={"deathstalkers","ghouls","ivar patch","ivar the foul","pumpkin patch","quinn yorick","rane yorick","silverpine forest"},["n"]="Ivar Patch",["s"]="The Ivar Patch is a blighted pumpkin farm located in northern Silverpine Forest. Once a thriving agricultural homestead of Lordaeron, its residents were wiped out during the Third War and transformed into ravenous, mindlessly hostile ghouls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War swept through Lordaeron, this pumpkin patch was a prosperous homestead owned by a farmer named Ivar, who employed a lively crew of farmhands and servants. When the Scourge unleashed the Plague of Undeath across the countryside, the farm was consumed completely. Rather than rising with their minds intact like the free-willed Forsaken, Ivar, his family, and his laborers were reduced to rotting, feral ghouls bound to prowl the ruined soil.",["t"]="A Ruined Harvest"},{["b"]="When the Forsaken began securing northern Silverpine, three Deathstalkers—Rane Yorick, Quinn Yorick, and Erland McKree—scouted the region to evaluate local threats. Passing through the Dead Field, the patrol was ambushed by the feral pack at the patch. Quinn was badly mauled by Ivar himself, now known as Ivar the Foul. With Quinn gravely wounded, the Yoricks fortified themselves inside the farm's old ruined house while McKree pressed on alone toward Malden's Orchard.",["t"]="The Deathstalker Ambush"}}}}}
t["subzone:jaggedswine-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,287,26.461.0,16.432.0,40.145.0,42.139.0,41.213.0,41.171.0",["h"]="0d4155",["n"]="La Pocilga",["s"]="La Pocilga. La Pocilga es una modesta granja de ganado situada en el norte de Durotar, justo al sur de la entrada principal de Orgrimmar. Compuesta por un cobertizo de almacenamiento de madera, un extenso corral y una charca enfangada, sirve como una fuente de alimento crucial que cría resistentes cerdos para la cercana capital de la Horda. Excavada en la implacable y calcinada tierra de Durotar, La Pocilga representa la dura realidad de mantener una fortaleza urbana como Orgrimmar. La tierra roja de la región ofrece una agricultura escasa, lo que hace que el ganado robusto sea esencial para alimentar a miles de guerreros y trabajadores orcos. La granja se articula en torno a un almacén de madera, un amplio corral de estacas y una charca natural donde se pastorea, cría y sacrifica a los cerdos para mantener abastecidos los graneros de la Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Establishing stable meat supplies in the arid wastes of Durotar is a matter of survival, making outposts like Jaggedswine vital to sustaining Orgrimmar's military strength.",["profession:Cooking"]="For Horde cooks learning their trade in Durotar, the abundant swine around Jaggedswine Farm make it a primary local source for tender ribs, pork cuts, and cooking grease."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farm raises and maintains swine to provide meat and lard for the Horde, particularly to feed the population and garrison of nearby Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"what is jaggedswine farm","why is there a pig farm in durotar","jaggedswine farm purpose"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Jaggedswine Farm?"},{["a"]="It lies in northern Durotar, sitting just outside the southern approach and grand gates that lead into the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"where is jaggedswine farm","how to get to jaggedswine farm","pig farm durotar location"},["q"]="Where exactly is Jaggedswine Farm located?"},{["a"]="Orcish livestock farming in Durotar is utilitarian and unglamorous. Between free-roaming boars and sparse timber structures, the steading lacks grand homesteads, but it remains actively used by Horde supply lines.",["al"]={"is jaggedswine farm abandoned","who lives at jaggedswine farm","why no farmers"},["q"]="Why does the farm look somewhat deserted?"},{["a"]="While the domesticated swine inside the pens are docile, wild and mature boars roaming the outskirts can be aggressive if startled by young travelers or careless foragers.",["al"]={"are swine hostile","do pigs attack here","swine dangerous"},["q"]="Are the pigs here dangerous to travelers?"}},["kw"]={"boars","durotar","horde provisions","jaggedswine farm","orgrimmar","pig pen","pigs","swine"},["n"]="Jaggedswine Farm",["s"]="Jaggedswine Farm is a modest livestock steading situated in northern Durotar, just south of the main entrance to Orgrimmar. Comprising a timber storage shed, a sprawling pen, and a muddy watering hole, it serves as a critical food source raising hardy swine for the nearby Horde capital.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved out of Durotar's unforgiving, sunbaked earth, Jaggedswine Farm represents the harsh reality of sustaining an urban stronghold like Orgrimmar. The red soil of the region yields sparse agriculture, making robust livestock essential to feeding thousands of orcish warriors and laborers. The farm centers on a timber storehouse, a wide wooden pen, and a natural watering pond where swine are herded, bred, and butchered to keep the Horde's granaries stocked.",["t"]="Provisions for the Capital"},{["b"]="Though quiet and often appearing half-tended under the dry heat, the farm is a regular stomping ground for local swineherds and patrolling Orgrimmar Grunts. Wild and mature swine roam both inside and outside the enclosures, occasionally testing the patience of nearby guards. Sitting right on the threshold of the capital's valley approach, the plot remains an unassuming yet indispensable outpost in the daily logistics of Durotar.",["t"]="A Quiet Frontier"}}}}}
t["subzone:jangolode-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,217,20.391.0,27.177.0,32.120.0,40.228.0",["h"]="e1f904",["n"]="Mina de Jango",["s"]="Mina de Jango. La Mina de Jango es una rica excavación minera ubicada en las onduladas colinas de Páramos de Poniente. Antaño una fuente vital de mineral y materias primas para Ciudad de Ventormenta, la mina ha sido tomada por los bandidos de la Hermandad Defias. Antes de que Páramos de Poniente cayera en decadencia, la Mina de Jango proporcionaba un flujo constante de metales cruciales para la reconstrucción y el abastecimiento de Ciudad de Ventormenta. A medida que el orden civil se deterioró y el reino retiró sus guarniciones, la Hermandad Defias se hizo con el control del enclave para abastecer sus propias operaciones. Los bandidos ahora explotan las ricas vetas para sí mismos, defendiendo con fiereza su botín subterráneo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Reclaiming Westfall's resources is vital for stabilizing the kingdom, and driving the bandits out of Jangolode is one step toward restoring the region's prosperity.",["profession:Mining"]="The Jangolode Mine remains rich in basic copper and tin deposits, making it a lucrative stop for prospectors willing to fight past the subterranean pests."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is an excavation site in Westfall that historically supplied Stormwind City with essential minerals and metal ore. With regional defense weakened, it fell into hostile hands.",["al"]={"jangolode mine info","what is jangolode","jangolode westfall"},["q"]="What is the Jangolode Mine?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood holds the underground shafts, having driven out the original miners to feed their own operations.",["al"]={"who is in jangolode mine","jangolode mobs","who lives in jangolode"},["q"]="Who controls the mine right now?"},{["a"]="Stormwind is mired in political unrest and struggling to protect even its core borders. The kingdom lacks the troops to garrison Westfall's outlying mines, leaving the People's Militia and local adventurers to manage the threat.",["al"]={"why doesnt stormwind clear jangolode","stormwind garrison westfall","why abandon the mine"},["q"]="Why does Stormwind not reclaim the mine?"}},["kw"]={"defias brotherhood","jangolode","jangolode mine","kobold","stormwind","westfall"},["n"]="Jangolode Mine",["s"]="Jangolode Mine is a rich mineral excavation located in the rolling hills of Westfall. Once a vital source of ore and raw materials for Stormwind City, the mine has been seized by the bandits of the Defias Brotherhood.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before Westfall fell into decline, the Jangolode Mine provided a steady flow of metals crucial to the reconstruction and supply of Stormwind City. As civil order deteriorated and the kingdom withdrew its garrisons, the Defias Brotherhood seized control of the site to feed their own operations. The bandits now work the rich veins for themselves, fiercely defending their subterranean prize.",["t"]="A Plundered Resource"}}}}}
t["subzone:jasperlode-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,272,25.414.0,19.391.0,31.218.0,56.215.0,35.162.0,43.235.0",["h"]="e24fa2",["n"]="Cantera de Jaspe",["s"]="Cantera de Jaspe. La Cantera de Jaspe es una excavación de hierro y minerales situada en la zona centronorte del Bosque de Elwynn que antaño abastecía a Ciudad de Ventormenta con recursos vitales. En la actualidad, los pozos están invadidos por enjambres de kóbolds y letales arañas gigantes, lo que deja al mermado reino sin capacidad para recuperarla. Históricamente, la Cantera de Jaspe fue una de las operaciones mineras más productivas de Ventormenta, proporcionando una constante riqueza mineral junto a la cercana Mina Abisal. Como el ejército del reino apenas da abasto para hacer frente a las amenazas externas y a los disturbios, las guarniciones locales se han visto incapaces de proteger los pozos. Los kóbolds aprovecharon la oportunidad para excavar en su interior, expulsando a los mineros humanos y acumulando oro robado y velas de sebo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Securing raw metal from Jasperlode is vital to maintaining Stormwind's equipment supplies during a time when the kingdom's borders face constant peril.",["profession:Mining"]="Rich in mineral veins, Jasperlode remains an enticing target for prospectors willing to fight through kobold pickaxes and spider webs to stake a claim."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Stormwind's standing army is spread thin across the realm, leaving rural outposts like Goldshire short on manpower. Opportunistic kobolds quickly swarmed the dig sites once the human miners lost their guard protection.",["al"]={"why are there kobolds","who controls jasperlode","why abandoned"},["q"]="Why is Jasperlode Mine overrun?"},{["a"]="Fargodeep Mine lies to the south near the Maclure and Stonefield farms, while Jasperlode sits to the north nestled in the foothills near the river. Both are major Elwynn mineral sites lost to the kobold infestation.",["al"]={"jasperlode vs fargodeep","other elwynn mine"},["q"]="What is the difference between Jasperlode and Fargodeep?"},{["a"]="The deepest shafts are infested with predatory mine spiders led by a massive arachnid known as Mother Fang. Even the occupying kobolds avoid their webbed caverns.",["al"]={"spiders in jasperlode","mother fang","what is at the bottom"},["q"]="What lurks in the back of the mine?"},{["a"]="Marshal Dughan lacks the troops to mount a prolonged subterranean clearing. Between Defias river patrols, gnoll incursions, and garrison duties, the local militia must rely on traveling adventurers to scout and cull the threats inside.",["al"]={"why no stormwind guard","dughan sending soldiers"},["q"]="Why hasn't Marshal Dughan cleared the mine?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","fargodeep","gold dust","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","marshal dughan","mother fang"},["n"]="Jasperlode Mine",["s"]="Jasperlode Mine is an iron and mineral excavation in north-central Elwynn Forest that once supplied Stormwind City with vital resources. Today, the shafts are overrun by swarming kobolds and deadly giant spiders, leaving the resource-strapped kingdom unable to reclaim it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Jasperlode Mine was historically one of Stormwind's most productive mining operations, providing steady mineral wealth alongside nearby Fargodeep. With the kingdom's military stretched thin defending against external threats and unrest, local garrisons have been unable to protect the shafts. Kobolds seized the opportunity to burrow inside, driving human miners out and stockpiling stolen gold and tallow candles.",["t"]="A Lost Resource in Elwynn"},{["b"]="The infestation within Jasperlode extends beyond simple vermin. In the deepest, darkest corridors beneath the timber supports, an aggressive colony of mine spiders has taken root. Led by a massive matriarch known to locals as Mother Fang, the spiders treat trespassing kobolds—and any unwary prospectors—as effortless prey, making any attempt to salvage the mine exceptionally hazardous.",["t"]="Dangers in the Deep"}}}}}
t["subzone:jerod-s-landing"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,255,21.490.0,19.384.1,33.175.0,29.163.0,48.194.0,42.163.0",["h"]="7e3a35",["n"]="Embarcadero de Jerod",["s"]="Embarcadero de Jerod. El Embarcadero de Jerod es un modesto muelle fluvial situado en la orilla del río Nazferiti correspondiente al Bosque de Elwynn. Actualmente tomado por la Hermandad Defias, este puesto de avanzada sirve como punto de transferencia clandestino para cargamentos ilícitos que se introducen de contrabando a través de las vías fluviales del reino. Escondido a lo largo de las aguas orientales del río Nazferiti, el Embarcadero de Jerod proporciona acceso fluvial que conecta el Bosque de Elwynn con los territorios vecinos. Aunque en su origen era un simple muelle para botes, el lugar ha caído firmemente en manos de la Hermandad Defias. Bajo la atenta mirada de un maestro de dársena Defias, los forajidos utilizan el muelle como centro para recibir mercancías saqueadas en las Montañas Crestagrana, trasladando discretamente los cargamentos río abajo hacia posesiones como La torre de Klaven en los Páramos de Poniente.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Rogues working on behalf of SI:7 are dispatched to Jerod's Landing to test their stealth, pickpocket the Defias dockmaster, and recover sensitive trade ledgers.",["faction:Alliance"]="The occupation of Jerod's Landing highlights how thoroughly the Defias have compromised the interior waterways linking Elwynn to Redridge right beneath Stormwind's nose."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Jerod's Landing is located in eastern Elwynn Forest, resting along the western bank of the Nazferiti River, which marks the boundary between Elwynn and the Redridge Mountains.",["al"]={"jerods landing location","where is jerod's landing","jerod dock map"},["q"]="Where is Jerod's Landing located?"},{["a"]="The landing has been occupied by members of the Defias Brotherhood, led by a Defias dockmaster who coordinates shipments with armed bandits guarding the waterside.",["al"]={"who is at jerods landing","defias at jerods landing","jerod landing mobs"},["q"]="Who controls Jerod's Landing?"},{["a"]="The Brotherhood utilizes the dock as a smuggling waystation to transport stolen goods and weaponry intercepted in the Redridge Mountains toward rogue strongholds like Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",["al"]={"why do defias use jerods landing","defias river smuggling"},["q"]="What is the purpose of this dock for the Defias?"},{["a"]="Master Mathias Shaw and his intelligence agents track the flow of Defias contraband through this dock to expose the network linking Westfall, Elwynn, and Redridge.",["al"]={"si7 jerods landing","rogue quest jerods landing"},["q"]="Why is SI:7 interested in Jerod's Landing?"}},["kw"]={"defias dockmaster","jerod's landing","klaven's tower","mathias shaw","nazferiti river","smuggling","snatch and grab"},["n"]="Jerod's Landing",["s"]="Jerod's Landing is a modest river dock situated on the Elwynn Forest bank of the Nazferiti River. Currently seized by the Defias Brotherhood, the outpost serves as a clandestine transfer point for illicit shipments smuggled across the kingdom's waterways.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away along the eastern waters of the Nazferiti River, Jerod's Landing provides river access connecting Elwynn Forest to neighboring territories. While originally an ordinary boat dock, the site has fallen firmly into the hands of the Defias Brotherhood. Under the watchful eye of a Defias dockmaster, outlaws utilize the dock as a hub to receive goods plundered from the Redridge Mountains, discreetly moving river cargo downstream toward holdings such as Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",["t"]="A Smuggler's Waypoint"},{["b"]="Because of its strategic placement on the river, Jerod's Landing has drawn the attention of SI:7, Stormwind's covert intelligence network. Operatives monitoring Defias operations view the landing as a vital link in the syndicate's supply lines, sending resourceful rogues to infiltrate the docks, pilfer river shipment ledgers, and unravel the wider conspiracy strangling the kingdom.",["t"]="Eyes in the Shadows"}}}}}
t["subzone:kargathia-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,261,26.521.0,22.373.0,32.129.0,19.158.0,33.195.0,49.185.0",["h"]="bd1bb9",["n"]="Fuerte de Kargathia",["s"]="Fuerte de Kargathia. El Fuerte de Kargathia es un bastión fortificado de la Horda que afianza el frente oriental del Aserradero Grito de Guerra en Vallefresno. Al servir como cuartel general de los capataces del puesto de avanzada, vigila la frontera fluvial y garantiza líneas de refuerzo rápido directas a Orgrimmar. Encaramado en el extremo oriental del Aserradero Grito de Guerra, justo al oeste del Río Furia del Sur, el Fuerte de Kargathia sirve como Centro de Mando para las operaciones madereras de la Horda en Vallefresno. Mejorado con pesadas barricadas de púas, este puesto fortificado alberga al Capataz Gorthak y a sus oficiales. Su posición estratégica junto a la frontera fluvial permite al clan Grito de Guerra vigilar las incursiones que se aproximan y recibir refuerzos rápidos directamente desde las tierras vecinas de Durotar y Orgrimmar siempre que atacan las escaramuzas de los elfos de la noche.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde defenders, Kargathia Keep is an indispensable sanctuary on the frontline of Ashenvale, securing valuable timber shipments vital to Orgrimmar's construction.",["race:NightElf"]="To the night elves, this heavily spiked stronghold represents the aggressive, deeply entrenched nature of the Horde's intrusion into their sacred ancestral forest."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kargathia Keep is situated in eastern Ashenvale, on the eastern edge of the Warsong Lumber Camp just west of the Southfury River.",["al"]={"kargathia keep location","where is kargathia keep","kargathia outpost location"},["q"]="Where is Kargathia Keep located?"},{["a"]="Overseer Gorthak commands the Warsong Lumber Camp from within Kargathia Keep, directing logging operations and coordinating defenses against Alliance attacks.",["al"]={"who is in charge of kargathia keep","kargathia keep leader","overseer gorthak"},["q"]="Who leads the keep?"},{["a"]="The stronghold was named in honor of Kargath Bladefist, the legendary chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan, sharing this naming heritage with Kargath in the Badlands and Bladefist Bay in Durotar.",["al"]={"who is kargathia keep named after","kargath bladefist","why kargathia"},["q"]="Why was the keep named Kargathia?"},{["a"]="The keep commands the eastern border of the logging camp along the Southfury River, securing the vital supply route and enabling rapid troop reinforcements to cross over from Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"why is kargathia keep here","purpose of kargathia keep","kargathia keep importance"},["q"]="What is the strategic purpose of this stronghold?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","kargath bladefist","kargathia keep","kargathia outpost","overseer gorthak","southfury river","warsong lumber camp"},["n"]="Kargathia Keep",["s"]="Kargathia Keep is a fortified Horde stronghold anchoring the eastern front of the Warsong Lumber Camp in Ashenvale. Serving as headquarters for the outpost's overseers, it guards the river border and ensures rapid reinforcement lines directly back to Orgrimmar.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the eastern edge of the Warsong Lumber Camp just west of the Southfury River, Kargathia Keep serves as the command center for the Horde's logging operations in Ashenvale. Upgraded with heavy spiked barricades, this fortified outpost houses Overseer Gorthak and his officers. Its strategic position against the river border allows the Warsong clan to monitor incoming incursions and receive swift reinforcements directly from the neighboring lands of Durotar and Orgrimmar whenever night elf skirmishers strike.",["t"]="A Bastion on the Southfury"},{["b"]="Like the fortress of Kargath in the Badlands and Bladefist Bay along the coast of Durotar, the outpost takes its name from the famed chieftain Kargath Bladefist. For the Warsong orcs braving Ashenvale's hostile woodlands, the keep's imposing classic architecture stands as an enduring symbol of martial resilience and Horde defiance in territory claimed by the night elves.",["t"]="Honoring the Bladefist"}}}}}
t["subzone:kodo-rock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,395,22.444.0,22.386.0,27.206.0,30.240.0,45.214.0,32.197.0",["h"]="0f93b2",["n"]="Roca de los Kodos",["s"]="Roca de los Kodos. La Roca de los Kodos es un monumento de piedra natural situado en las llanuras de la Mesa de la Nube Roja, entre el Campamento Narache y el Barranco Cortazarza. Alzándose en silencio entre las hierbas de Mulgore, sirve como un temprano lugar de peregrinación para los jóvenes chamanes tauren que aprenden a comunicarse con los espíritus de la tierra. Debido a su modesta silueta frente al ondulado paisaje, los viajeros deben afinar la vista para avistarla. Situada aproximadamente a mitad de camino por el sendero que conecta el Campamento Narache con el hostil territorio jabaespín del Barranco Cortazarza, la Roca de los Kodos se distingue por una parcela de tierra desgastada en su base. Aunque carece de la imponente grandeza de los elevados riscos que rodean la Mesa de la Nube Roja, su perfil característico recuerda a las veneradas bestias kodo que recorren las praderas. Para los miembros de las tribus errantes, actúa como una apacible baliza natural en las ventosas llanuras de Mulgore.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="For novice tauren shamans beginning their spiritual path at Camp Narache, Kodo Rock is a vital landmark used to attune with the elemental world.",["race:Tauren"]="The stone formation serves as a familiar landmark across the plains of Red Cloud Mesa, reflecting the sacred bond between the Shu'halo and the beasts of Mulgore."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kodo Rock is situated on Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore. You can find it roughly halfway along a straight path between Camp Narache and Brambleblade Ravine, marked on the ground by a small clearing of bare dirt.",["al"]={"kodo rock location","where is kodo rock","find kodo rock"},["q"]="Where is Kodo Rock located?"},{["a"]="The monument blends naturally into the rolling hills and grasses of the mesa. It is only clearly visible from a relatively short distance, requiring travelers to pay close attention to the terrain and watch for the patch of dirt beneath it.",["al"]={"cant find kodo rock","kodo rock hidden"},["q"]="Why is Kodo Rock hard to find?"},{["a"]="Tauren shamans visit the rock during their earliest trials out of Camp Narache. It serves as a peaceful, sacred landmark for novices learning to attune their spirits to the land and the elemental forces of Mulgore.",["al"]={"shaman quest kodo rock","why go to kodo rock"},["q"]="Why is Kodo Rock important to tauren shamans?"},{["a"]="While the immediate patch around Kodo Rock is generally peaceful, heading further northeast leads directly toward Brambleblade Ravine, a canyon densely populated by aggressive Bristleback quilboar.",["al"]={"is kodo rock safe","enemies near kodo rock"},["q"]="What dangers are near Kodo Rock?"}},["kw"]={"brambleblade ravine","camp narache","kodo rock","monument","mulgore","red cloud mesa","shaman trial","tauren shaman"},["n"]="Kodo Rock",["s"]="Kodo Rock is a natural stone monument located in the plains of Red Cloud Mesa, between Camp Narache and Brambleblade Ravine. Standing quietly amid the grasses of Mulgore, it serves as an early pilgrimage site for young tauren shamans learning to commune with the spirits of the earth. Because of its modest silhouette against the rolling landscape, travelers must keep a keen eye out to spot it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated roughly halfway along the path connecting Camp Narache to the hostile quillboar territory of Brambleblade Ravine, Kodo Rock is marked by a patch of worn earth at its base. While it lacks the sheer grandeur of the towering bluffs surrounding Red Cloud Mesa, its distinct profile resembles the revered kodo beasts that wander the grasslands. For wandering tribesfolk, it acts as a quiet natural beacon in the windswept plains of Mulgore.",["t"]="A Waypoint on the Mesa"},{["b"]="To the Shu'halo, natural formations often carry spiritual weight. Kodo Rock holds special reverence for young tauren shamans beginning their spiritual walk. Novices are directed here on early rites of passage, using the solitary stone monument as a sacred grounds to commune with elemental forces and honor the natural world before venturing into more perilous reaches of the continent.",["t"]="Spiritual Significance"}}}}}
t["subzone:kolkar-crag"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,219,25.544.0,19.461.1,25.181.0,45.217.0,27.170.0",["h"]="ec887c",["n"]="Risco Kolkar",["s"]="Risco Kolkar. Risco Kolkar es un desfiladero escarpado y abrasado por el sol situado en el sur de Durotar, reclamado por los hostiles centauros Kolkar. Liderado por el señor de la guerra Kolkanis, este enclave sirve como base de operaciones para incursiones coordinadas contra los asentamientos cercanos de la Horda. Oculto entre los abruptos cañones del sur de Durotar, Risco Kolkar es una base de operaciones para el agresivo clan Kolkar. A pesar del terreno árido e implacable, estos centauros han fortificado los pasos estrechos naturales del desfiladero. Desde este barranco, sus exploradores y merodeadores vigilan de cerca las llanuras circundantes, buscando puntos débiles en las posesiones de los orcos y los Lanza Negra. Para los jóvenes guerreros que entrenan en el Valle de los Retos o patrullan la costa sur, Risco Kolkar representa el frente organizado de hostilidad de los centauros más cercano.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Securing southern Durotar against centaur incursions protects the supply lines running between Sen'jin Village and the road to Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="The presence of centaur so close to the Valley of Trials threatens the initiation of young orcs, making the pacification of Kolkar Crag an urgent matter of territorial defense."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kolkar Crag is held by the Kolkar centaur clan, led on-site by Warlord Kolkanis. They use the defensible canyon as a camp and raiding post against Horde outposts throughout Durotar.",["al"]={"who is at kolkar crag","kolkar crag inhabitants","who owns kolkar crag"},["q"]="Who lives in Kolkar Crag?"},{["a"]="The centaur within the gorge have drafted plans to launch coordinated assaults on Durotar's vital settlements, including the training grounds in the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and Orgrimmar itself.",["al"]={"why care about kolkar crag","is kolkar crag dangerous","kolkar threat"},["q"]="Why is the Horde concerned about this ravine?"},{["a"]="The encampment is commanded by Warlord Kolkanis, a ferocious centaur warlord who directs their scouting maneuvers and formulates battle plans against the orcs and trolls.",["al"]={"kolkar crag boss","who leads kolkar crag","warlord kolkanis"},["q"]="Who leads the centaur here?"}},["kw"]={"centaur","durotar","kolkanis","kolkar","kolkar crag","sen'jin village","valley of trials","warlord kolkanis"},["n"]="Kolkar Crag",["s"]="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked, jagged gorge in southern Durotar claimed by the hostile Kolkar centaur. Led by Warlord Kolkanis, this enclave serves as a staging ground for coordinated raids against nearby Horde settlements.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the rugged canyons of southern Durotar, Kolkar Crag is a base of operations for the aggressive Kolkar clan. Despite the arid and unforgiving terrain, these centaur have fortified the natural choke points of the gorge. From this ravine, their scouts and marauders keep close watch over the surrounding flats, probing for vulnerabilities across orc and Darkspear holdings. For young warriors training in the Valley of Trials or patrolling the southern coast, Kolkar Crag represents the nearest organized front of centaur hostility.",["t"]="A Thorn in Durotar's Side"},{["b"]="Under the command of Warlord Kolkanis, the centaur entrenched at the crag hold ambitions far beyond simple skirmishes. Recovered attack plans reveal plots targeting the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and daring strikes aimed directly toward the gates of Orgrimmar. Halting these plans requires decisive preemptive strikes deep into the ravine to assassinate Kolkanis and break their muster before their war parties can sweep through the valleys.",["t"]="Schemes of Invasion"}}}}}
t["subzone:lake-al-ameth"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,291,20.551.0,18.386.0,31.96.0,51.198.0,45.136.0,18.173.0",["h"]="87b28f",["n"]="Lago Al'Ameth",["s"]="Lago Al'Ameth. El Lago Al'Ameth es una de las mayores masas de agua dulce situadas en lo alto de las ramas de Teldrassil, justo al sur de Dolanaar. Aunque antaño fue un remanso de paz que apenas contaba con un sencillo embarcadero de madera, sus orillas se han vuelto peligrosas debido a la violenta agitación de la vegetación local. Situado inmediatamente al sur de la aldea de Dolanaar, el Lago Al'Ameth actúa como una cuenca natural vital en el corazón de Teldrassil. A pesar de sus aguas serenas y sus escasos asentamientos, la paz aquí se ha esfumado. Enjambres de brezomaderas agitados y Brotes de Brezomadera merodean por la orilla, enloquecidos por una enfermedad antinatural que se propaga por el Árbol del Mundo. Los druidas e investigadores de Dolanaar envían con frecuencia a viajeros a estas orillas para recoger semillas y abatir a las agresivas criaturas antes de que la corrupción penetre más profundamente en el bosque circundante.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The wild timberlings around the lake offer druids a hands-on study of the unnatural corruption undermining Teldrassil's flora and fauna.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth is an alarming sign of the ailments troubling their newly raised home, forcing young defenders to protect the surrounding road."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lake Al'Ameth lies directly south of the night elf settlement of Dolanaar in eastern Teldrassil.",["al"]={"lake alameth location","where is lake al'ameth","find lake al'ameth"},["q"]="Where is Lake Al'Ameth located?"},{["a"]="The timberlings and plant life along the shores have fallen victim to a corrupting sickness afflicting Teldrassil, driving previously harmless woodland spriggans and treants into a territorial rage.",["al"]={"why timberlings angry","lake alameth enemies","aggressive timberlings"},["q"]="Why are the creatures around Lake Al'Ameth hostile?"},{["a"]="The lake is largely wild and undeveloped, featuring only a simple wooden fishing jetty on its northern bank near the path from Dolanaar.",["al"]={"lake alameth pier","dock at lake alameth"},["q"]="What structures or landmarks are on the lake?"},{["a"]="Oakenscowl is a powerful, corrupted ancient lurking near the groves of Lake Al'Ameth. He serves as an embodiment of the violent rot warping the forest creatures in the area.",["al"]={"what is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lake al'ameth"},["q"]="Who is Oakenscowl?"}},["kw"]={"dolanaar","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling","timberling seeds"},["n"]="Lake Al'Ameth",["s"]="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest freshwater bodies nestled high in the boughs of Teldrassil, located just south of Dolanaar. Though once a tranquil haven featuring little more than a simple wooden jetty, its shores have grown perilous due to the violent agitation of the local plant life.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Resting immediately south of the village of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth serves as a vital natural basin in the heart of Teldrassil. Despite its serene waters and minimal settlement, peace here has evaporated. Swarms of agitated timberlings and timberling sprouts prowl the water's edge, driven mad by an unnatural sickness spreading through the world tree. Druids and researchers from Dolanaar frequently dispatch travelers to these shores to gather seeds and cull the aggressive creatures before the corruption spreads deeper into the surrounding forest.",["t"]="A Troubled Shoreline"},{["b"]="The hostility around Lake Al'Ameth is directly tied to the woodland spirits losing their balance. Massive, corrupted treants like Oakenscowl lurk in the nearby groves, while natural timberlings lash out at any who approach. For the Cenarion Circle, diagnosing and treating the rot around Lake Al'Ameth is an urgent test of whether Teldrassil's unblessed creation can truly be sustained.",["t"]="The Roots of Wrath"}}}}}
t["subzone:lake-falathim"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,369,19.413.0,27.352.0,31.125.0,48.215.0,32.146.0,16.163.0",["h"]="f379a8",["n"]="Lago Falathim",["s"]="Lago Falathim. El Lago Falathim es una tranquila masa de agua ubicada en las boscosas colinas del oeste de Vallefresno, al suroeste de la Atalaya de Maestra. Venerado por el constante roce de la luz de la luna de Elune sobre su superficie tanto de día como de noche, antaño fue un apreciado retiro para los elfos de la noche. En los últimos tiempos, sin embargo, agresivos múrlocs han invadido sus orillas, transformando un refugio sagrado en un peligro constante. Escondido al sureste de La Ensenada de Zoram, el Lago Falathim fue apreciado durante mucho tiempo por los Kaldorei como un santuario pacífico para nadar y pescar. Según las leyendas locales, el suave resplandor de Elune descansa sobre estas aguas a todas horas, sea de día o de noche. A pesar de esta sagrada bendición, feroces múrlocs han avanzado tierra adentro para apoderarse de las costas, anidando en gran número y ahuyentando tanto a viajeros locales como a eruditos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts out of Maestra's Post keep a watchful eye toward Lake Falathim, wary of murloc incursions and seeking word on lost scholars like Teronis.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, Lake Falathim is a reminder of wilderness sanctity under siege, where an idyllic lake touched by Elune's constant moonlight is desecrated by savage murloc tribes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lake Falathim lies in western Ashenvale, tucked into the hills southwest of Maestra's Post and southeast of the Zoram Strand.",["al"]={"lake falathim location","where is lake falathim","find lake falathim"},["q"]="Where is Lake Falathim located?"},{["a"]="The lake holds spiritual significance because the goddess Elune's moonlight is said to perpetually touch its waters, whether by day or by night. Historically, night elves visited its peaceful banks to fish and swim.",["al"]={"why is lake falathim important","lake falathim lore","moonlight lake ashenvale"},["q"]="Why is Lake Falathim special to the night elves?"},{["a"]="The lake has been infested by hostile murlocs that have migrated up from the nearby coastal regions, making the shoreline dangerous for travelers.",["al"]={"lake falathim mobs","what is at lake falathim","lake falathim monsters"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit the lake?"},{["a"]="Teronis was a night elf scholar who ventured out near Lake Falathim and went missing, with his disappearance attributed to the vicious murlocs inhabiting the area.",["al"]={"teronis lake falathim","who is teronis","missing scholar lake falathim"},["q"]="Who was Teronis?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","elune","falathim","lake falathim","maestra's post","moonlight","murloc","teronis"},["n"]="Lake Falathim",["s"]="Lake Falathim is a tranquil body of water nestled in the forested hills of western Ashenvale, southwest of Maestra's Post. Revered for the constant touch of Elune's moonlight upon its surface day and night, it was once a beloved retreat for night elves. In recent days, however, aggressive murlocs have overrun its shores, turning a sacred haven into a perilous hazard.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away southeast of the Zoram Strand, Lake Falathim was long cherished by the Kaldorei as a peaceful sanctuary for swimming and fishing. According to local lore, the gentle radiance of Elune rests upon these waters at all hours, day or night. Despite this sacred blessing, ferocious murlocs have surged inland to seize the shores, nesting in thick numbers and driving away local travelers and scholars alike.",["t"]="Bathed in Moonlight"},{["b"]="The sudden occupation by murlocs has made the lake deadly to solitary wanderers. The night elf scholar Teronis was recently lost somewhere near the water's edge on a mission of inquiry. Given the savage hostility of the amphibians lurking on the banks and in the shallows, the Sentinels fear the worst for any who venture toward the moonlit pool alone.",["t"]="The Scholar's Disappearance"}}}}}
